# Working in \`.spectacular/\`

This is the onboarding doc for any agent or human landing inside this workspace. Read this first.

## What this folder is

\`.spectacular/\` is an AI-native operational workspace for **${name}**. It separates four things deliberately:

| Layer | Files | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Intent | \`PRD.md\` | What we want and why |
| Truth | \`SPEC.md\` + \`specs/\` | What's built right now (SPEC.md is the always-on index) |
| Work | \`requests/<slug>/\` | What's changing next (PLAN.md owns lifecycle state) |
| Memory | \`memory/\` | What we learned, kept across sessions |

Optional canonical docs (\`PRINCIPLES.md\`, \`ARCHITECTURE.md\`, \`ROADMAP.md\`, \`STACK.md\`, \`DECISIONS.md\`) are scaffolded by kits — not every project needs them.

## How to operate

1. **Read frontmatter first**, file bodies second. \`status:\`, \`summary:\`, \`version:\`, \`updated:\`, \`related:\` are the navigation layer.
2. **Load progressively.** The top-level \`SPEC.md\` is cheap and always relevant. Don't pre-load all of \`specs/\` or \`requests/\` — load only what the current task needs (see Context loading below).
3. **Snapshot before overwrite** on any canonical doc — root layer, \`SPEC.md\`, \`specs/<capability>/SPEC.md\`, \`config.yaml\`. Naming: \`<FILE>@vN.md\`. The unversioned filename always points to current. Use \`spectacular snapshot <file>\` to do it.
4. **Propose, don't act** on irreversibles — archives, lifecycle promotions, memory writes, bulk edits >5 files. Confirm with the human first.
5. **Never read \`archive/\`** during normal operation. It's write-only from your perspective.
6. **Write to \`memory/\` only on explicit confirmation** via \`spectacular remember this\`. Never autonomously.

## Context loading by task

Load the minimum needed for the task — don't slurp the whole workspace.

| Task type | Load |
|---|---|
| Cold onboarding | \`PRD.md\`, \`SPEC.md\`, this file |
| Planning a new request | \`PRD.md\`, \`SPEC.md\`, \`PRINCIPLES.md\` (if present), \`DECISIONS.md\` (if present) |
| Refining intent / PRD work | \`PRD.md\` + relevant skill refs |
| Implementing a request | \`STACK.md\` (if present), \`requests/<slug>/PLAN.md\`, \`TASKS.md\`, \`SPEC.md\`, the specific \`specs/<capability>/SPEC.md\` files the work touches |
| Reviewing / QA | \`requests/<slug>/VERIFY.md\` (if present), affected \`specs/<capability>/SPEC.md\`, \`RISKS.md\` (if present) |
| Structural questions | \`ARCHITECTURE.md\` only (if present) |

## Task tracking — two layers

| Layer | Tool | Use for |
|---|---|---|
| Session micro-steps | Harness \`TaskCreate\` / \`TaskUpdate\` | Ephemeral per-session steps — drives the CLI live progress UI |
| Persistent milestones | On-disk \`requests/<slug>/TASKS.md\` | Stable milestone blocks that survive across sessions |

Anti-pattern: 1:1 duplication between the two layers. Use the harness for the granular checklist *within* a milestone block; use TASKS.md for the milestones themselves.

## Available skills

- \`/spectacular\` — workspace orchestration (briefings, requests, lifecycle, archive, memory, doc verbs)

Add other project skills here as they're installed.

## Creating requests

\`\`\`bash
spectacular new <description>
\`\`\`

The skill derives a kebab-case slug, applies the verification 2-of-6 rule to decide whether to scaffold a \`VERIFY.md\`, and asks for confirmation before writing.

> **Anti-pattern:** never create \`requests/<slug>/PRD.md\`. Product intent is project-wide and lives at \`.spectacular/PRD.md\`. Per-request \`PLAN.md\` references it.

## Don'ts

- Don't touch \`archive/\` during normal operation
- Don't overwrite canonical docs in place — snapshot first
- Don't write to \`memory/\` autonomously
- Don't create per-request PRDs
- Don't commit \`.spectacular.local/\` (it's personal + gitignored)
"
}

doc_gitignore() {
  local gitignore=".gitignore"
  if [[ -f "$gitignore" ]]; then
    if grep -qF ".spectacular.local/" "$gitignore"; then
      skip ".gitignore (already contains .spectacular.local/)"
    else
      echo ".spectacular.local/" >> "$gitignore"
      info "  ✓  updated .gitignore (.spectacular.local/ added)"
    fi
  else
    printf '.spectacular.local/\n' > "$gitignore"
    created ".gitignore"
  fi
  # Returns 1 when already in sync — that's a status, not an error; don't let
  # `set -e` treat it as fatal during init.
  snapshot_gitignore_sync || true
}

# Add or remove the snapshot-store ignore line in .gitignore to match the
# `snapshots.gitignore` config (b16). Default false → store stays in git. Idempotent.
# Returns 0 if it changed the file, 1 if already in sync.
snapshot_gitignore_sync() {
  local gitignore=".gitignore"
  local entry="$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/$(config_snapshots_folder)/"
  local want; want="$(config_snapshots_gitignore)"
  [[ -f "$gitignore" ]] || { [[ "$want" == "true" ]] || return 1; touch "$gitignore"; }
  local present=1; grep -qxF "$entry" "$gitignore" 2>/dev/null || present=0
  if [[ "$want" == "true" && "$present" -eq 0 ]]; then
    echo "$entry" >> "$gitignore"; return 0
  elif [[ "$want" == "false" && "$present" -eq 1 ]]; then
    # grep -v exits 1 when it filters out every line (empty result) — don't gate mv on it.
    grep -vxF "$entry" "$gitignore" > "$gitignore.tmp" || true
    mv "$gitignore.tmp" "$gitignore"; return 0
  fi
  return 1
}

# Parse a pack's gitignore.always-add list from its pack.md frontmatter.
# Args: $1 = absolute path to a pack folder
# Stdout: one entry per line
pack_gitignore_always_add() {
  local pack_dir="$1"
  local manifest="${pack_dir}/pack.md"
  [[ -f "$manifest" ]] || return 0
  awk '
    /^---$/ { fm++; if (fm==2) exit; next }
    fm==1 && /^  gitignore:/ { in_gi=1; next }
    fm==1 && in_gi && /^  [a-z]/ { in_gi=0 }
    fm==1 && in_gi && /^    always-add:/ { in_aa=1; next }
    fm==1 && in_gi && in_aa && /^    [a-z]/ { in_aa=0 }
    fm==1 && in_gi && in_aa && /^      - / {
      v=$0; sub(/^      - /, "", v); gsub(/[[:space:]]*$/, "", v); print v
    }
  ' "$manifest"
}

# Apply the active pack's scaffold to the project, when mode allows.
# Currently: appends gitignore.always-add entries (deduplicated).
# Always-set wins on conflicts (gitignore append never overwrites existing lines).
pack_apply_scaffold() {
  local pack_src="$1"   # resolved pack folder
  local mode="$2"       # suggest | scaffold | enforce
  case "$mode" in
    scaffold|enforce) ;;
    *) return 0 ;;
  esac

  local gitignore=".gitignore"
  [[ -f "$gitignore" ]] || touch "$gitignore"

  local added=0
  while IFS= read -r entry; do
    [[ -z "$entry" ]] && continue
    if ! grep -qF -- "$entry" "$gitignore"; then
      echo "$entry" >> "$gitignore"
      added=$((added + 1))
    fi
  done < <(pack_gitignore_always_add "$pack_src")

  if [[ $added -gt 0 ]]; then
    info "  ✓  pack scaffold ($mode): appended $added gitignore entries from $(basename "$pack_src")"
  else
    skip "  pack scaffold ($mode): .gitignore already covered"
  fi
}

# ── scaffold orchestrator ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Resolves the doc-set per kit + flags, then dispatches to doc_<id>() functions.
scaffold() {
  local name="$1" summary="$2" agents_file="$3"
  local kit_id="${OPT_KIT:-blank}"
  local doc_set
  doc_set="$(resolve_doc_set)"

  echo "  kit:    $kit_id"
  echo "  docs:   $doc_set"
  echo ""

  # Always: dirs + gitignore
  doc_dirs
  doc_gitignore

  # Dispatch per-doc
  for doc in $doc_set; do
    case "$doc" in
      config)        doc_config "$name" "$summary" "$agents_file" "$kit_id" ;;
      prd)           doc_prd "$name" "$kit_id" ;;
      spec)          doc_spec "$name" ;;
      principles)    doc_principles "$name" ;;
      policy)        doc_policy "$name" ;;
      architecture)  doc_architecture "$name" ;;
      roadmap)       doc_roadmap "$name" ;;
      stack)         doc_stack ;;
      decisions)     doc_decisions ;;
      memory)        doc_memory ;;
      sessions)      doc_sessions ;;
      agents)        doc_agents "$name" "$agents_file" ;;
      personas)      doc_personas ;;
      findings)      doc_findings ;;
      fixes)         doc_fixes ;;
      bugs)          doc_bugs ;;
      security)      doc_security ;;
      benchmarks)    doc_benchmarks ;;
      *) die "Unknown doc ID in resolved set: '$doc'" ;;
    esac
  done

  # Convention pack: apply scaffold if config.yaml declares one and mode allows
  local pack_src_name pack_mode
  pack_src_name="$(config_pack_source)"
  if [[ -n "$pack_src_name" ]]; then
    pack_mode="$(config_pack_mode)"
    local pack_resolved
    if pack_resolved="$(pack_resolve "$pack_src_name")"; then
      pack_apply_scaffold "$pack_resolved" "$pack_mode"
    else
      info "  ⚠  convention_pack source '$pack_src_name' not found in any scope — skipped"
    fi
  fi
}

# ── print summary ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
print_summary() {
  local agents_dir claude_dir ref
  agents_dir="$(agents_skill_dir)"
  claude_dir="$(claude_skill_dir)"
  ref="${INSTALLED_REF:-}"

  echo ""
  echo "Spectacular initialized."
  echo ""
  echo "Run /spectacular to get started."
}

# ── main ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DOCTOR — environment / infrastructure self-check
#
# CLI detects substrate drift. Mechanical fixes (gitignore append, missing dirs,
# dangling symlinks, missing always-set stubs) can apply via --fix. Anything
# requiring judgment is reported as fix_type=judgment and routes to the skill
# (/spectacular doctor --fix). See references/doctor.md for the full spec.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── doctor globals ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DOC_OPT_AREA=""        # empty = all areas
DOC_OPT_FIX=false
DOC_OPT_FORMAT="text"  # text | json

DOC_AREAS="skill workspace frontmatter snapshots links lifecycle kits conventions specs docs personas memory sessions feedback ideas wayfinding debug fixes afk policies vision decisions roadmap"

# Findings accumulator. Each line:  area|severity|file|message|proposed_fix|fix_type
# severity: pass | warning | error | info
# fix_type: mechanical | judgment | none
DOC_FINDINGS=""

doc_add() {
  local area="$1" sev="$2" file="$3" msg="$4" fix="${5:-}" ftype="${6:-none}"
  DOC_FINDINGS+="${area}|${sev}|${file}|${msg}|${fix}|${ftype}"$'\n'
}

# ── usage block for doctor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
doctor_usage() {
  cat <<EOF
Usage: spectacular doctor [<area>] [options]

Run substrate self-check on the current .spectacular/ workspace.

Areas (run all if omitted):
  skill         skill install + symlinks + skills.lock
  workspace     .spectacular/ directory + always-set + config.yaml
  frontmatter   required fields per canonical doc; schema versions
  snapshots     version-sequence continuity (PRD@v1.0 + v1.2 without v1.1)
  links         related: frontmatter targets exist
  lifecycle     request status vs required verification artifacts
  kits          bundled + project-local kit files parse cleanly
  conventions   active convention_pack resolves; gitignore drift in scaffold/enforce modes
  specs         specs/index.md present + parseable; specs/ dir present; flat files; index drift vs newest archive
  docs          docs.yaml + frontmatter validation across the docs/ tree (v0.6.0+)
  personas      PERSONAS.md frontmatter + persona blocks + stories (v1.3.0+; opt-in)
  memory        memories/index.md frontmatter + index ↔ entries drift; prefix naming
  sessions      sessions/index.md frontmatter + open-session invariant + 4h stale warning
  feedback      feedbacks/ entries — frontmatter, stale-open (>30d), orphan back-refs
  ideas         ideas/ entries — frontmatter, stale-exploring (>90d), orphan promoted
  debug         debugs/<slug> trace spines — status/disposition enums
  fixes         fixes/ trusted corpus — concrete verification evidence
  afk           afk/runs/ authorization records — state, scope, and single-active invariant
  decisions     decisions/index.md index-mode consistency — orphans, stale files, prefix naming, numbering gaps

Options:
  --fix              Apply mechanical fixes (gitignore append, missing dirs,
                     dangling symlinks, missing always-set stubs). Judgment
                     fixes require the skill: /spectacular doctor --fix.
  --format text|json Report format (default: text). JSON suitable for the
                     skill or other tools to consume.
  -h, --help         Show this help

Exit codes: 0 clean, 1 warnings only, 2 errors present.

Examples:
  spectacular doctor
  spectacular doctor frontmatter
  spectacular doctor --fix
  spectacular doctor --format json > .spectacular/.doctor-report.json
EOF
}

doctor_parse_args() {
  while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do
    case "$1" in
      --fix) DOC_OPT_FIX=true; shift ;;
      --format) require_value "--format" "${2:-}"; DOC_OPT_FORMAT="$2"; shift 2 ;;
      -h|--help) doctor_usage; exit 0 ;;
      skill|workspace|frontmatter|snapshots|links|lifecycle|kits|conventions|specs|docs|personas|memory|sessions|feedback|ideas|wayfinding|debug|fixes|afk|policies|vision|decisions|roadmap)
        if [[ -z "$DOC_OPT_AREA" ]]; then
          DOC_OPT_AREA="$1"
        else
          DOC_OPT_AREA="$DOC_OPT_AREA $1"
        fi
        shift ;;
      *) die "Unknown doctor option: $1. Run 'spectacular doctor --help'." ;;
    esac
  done

  if [[ "$DOC_OPT_FORMAT" != "text" && "$DOC_OPT_FORMAT" != "json" ]]; then
    die "--format must be 'text' or 'json'"
  fi
}

# ── area: skill ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
check_skill() {
  local agents_dir claude_dir lock_ref
  agents_dir="$(agents_skill_dir)"
  claude_dir="$(claude_skill_dir)"

  # Install path
  if [[ -d "$agents_dir" || -L "$agents_dir" ]]; then
    doc_add "skill" "pass" "$agents_dir" "skill installed"
  else
    doc_add "skill" "error" "$agents_dir" "skill not installed at this path" \
      "re-run \`spectacular init\` (or \`spectacular init --update\`)" "judgment"
    return
  fi

  # Symlink validity. Only report a problem when .claude/ exists (user is
  # actively using Claude Code) but the symlink under it is missing/broken.
  # If .claude/ doesn't exist at all, the user isn't using Claude Code here
  # and there's nothing to fix.
  local claude_parent
  claude_parent=$(dirname "$claude_dir")
  if [[ -L "$claude_dir" ]]; then
    if [[ -e "$claude_dir" ]]; then
      doc_add "skill" "pass" "$claude_dir" "symlink resolves"
    else
      doc_add "skill" "error" "$claude_dir" "symlink is dangling (target missing)" \
        "recreate symlink to $agents_dir" "mechanical"
    fi
  elif [[ -d "$claude_parent" ]] && [[ ! -e "$claude_dir" ]]; then
    doc_add "skill" "warning" "$claude_dir" "no symlink found (claude dir exists but skill not symlinked here)" \
      "create symlink from $claude_dir to $agents_dir" "mechanical"
  fi

  # skills.lock present + parseable
  # If running in the spectacular source repo itself (where cli/spectacular lives),
  # missing skills.lock is expected — downgrade warning to info.
  local lock="$(pwd)/.spectacular/skills.lock"
  local is_source_repo=false
  if [[ -f "$(pwd)/cli/spectacular" && -d "$(pwd)/skills/spectacular" ]]; then
    is_source_repo=true
  fi
  if [[ -f "$lock" ]]; then
    if grep -q "^spectacular:" "$lock" 2>/dev/null || grep -q "ref:" "$lock" 2>/dev/null; then
      doc_add "skill" "pass" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/skills.lock" "skills.lock present"
    else
      doc_add "skill" "warning" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/skills.lock" "skills.lock present but no ref/version detected" "" "judgment"
    fi
  elif $is_source_repo; then
    doc_add "skill" "info" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/skills.lock" "absent (this is the spectacular source repo — expected)"
  else
    doc_add "skill" "warning" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/skills.lock" "missing (skill may not have been installed via CLI)" "" "judgment"
  fi

  # SKILL.md parseable
  local skill_md="$agents_dir/SKILL.md"
  if [[ -f "$skill_md" ]]; then
    if head -1 "$skill_md" | grep -q '^---$'; then
      doc_add "skill" "pass" "$skill_md" "SKILL.md frontmatter loads"
      # description length vs Codex's 1024-char cap. See scripts/check-skill-desc.sh
      # and .spectacular/decisions/D7.md — Codex measures `description` ALONE and
      # skips any skill over 1024. Claude Code's 1536 cap masks this, so a guard is
      # the only thing that catches it before a release ships.
      check_skill_desc_len "$skill_md"
    else
      doc_add "skill" "error" "$skill_md" "SKILL.md missing frontmatter delimiter" \
        "re-install the skill via \`spectacular init --update\`" "judgment"
    fi
  else
    doc_add "skill" "error" "$skill_md" "SKILL.md missing" \
      "re-install the skill via \`spectacular init --update\`" "judgment"
  fi
}

# Measure a SKILL.md `description` block (chars) and file a doctor finding.
# Thresholds: error > 1024 (Codex skips the skill), warning > 1000 (about to break).
# Kept in lock-step with scripts/check-skill-desc.sh (the pre-commit path).
check_skill_desc_len() {
  local skill_md="$1"
  local n
  n=$(awk '
    /^---$/ { fm = !fm; if (!fm && seen) exit; next }
    fm && /^description:[[:space:]]*\|[[:space:]]*$/ { in_desc=1; seen=1; next }
    fm && /^description:[[:space:]]*[^|[:space:]]/ {
      val = $0; sub(/^description:[[:space:]]*/, "", val); gsub(/^"|"$/, "", val)
      total += length(val); seen=1; exit
    }
    in_desc {
      if ($0 ~ /^[^[:space:]]/ || $0 ~ /^---$/) { exit }
      line = $0; sub(/^[[:space:]]+/, "", line)
      if (started) total += 1
      total += length(line); started=1
    }
    END { print total + 0 }
  ' "$skill_md")
  if (( n > 1024 )); then
    doc_add "skill" "error" "$skill_md" "description is $n chars — over Codex's 1024 cap (Codex will skip this skill)" \
      "trim the \`description\` frontmatter below 1024 chars" "judgment"
  elif (( n > 1000 )); then
    doc_add "skill" "warning" "$skill_md" "description is $n chars — $((1024 - n)) under the 1024 cap; trim soon" \
      "trim the \`description\` frontmatter to give more headroom" "judgment"
  else
    doc_add "skill" "pass" "$skill_md" "description length ok ($n chars, under 1024 Codex cap)"
  fi
}

# ── area: workspace ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
check_workspace() {
  if [[ ! -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]]; then
    doc_add "workspace" "error" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/" "directory missing — workspace not initialized" \
      "run \`spectacular init\`" "judgment"
    return
  fi
  doc_add "workspace" "pass" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/" "workspace directory present"

  # Always-set files (per smart-init's definition)
  # Determine which agents-file is in use by reading config.yaml first
  local agents_file="AGENTS.md"
  if [[ -f "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" ]]; then
    local cfg_agents
    cfg_agents=$(awk '/^  file:/ { print $2; exit }' "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" 2>/dev/null)
    [[ -n "$cfg_agents" ]] && agents_file="$cfg_agents"
  fi

  local always_set=("PRD.md" "config.yaml" "POLICY.md" "$agents_file")
  for f in "${always_set[@]}"; do
    if [[ -f "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/$f" ]]; then
      doc_add "workspace" "pass" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/$f" "always-set file present"
    else
      doc_add "workspace" "error" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/$f" "always-set file missing" \
        "re-scaffold via \`spectacular doctor --fix\` or \`spectacular init\`" "mechanical"
    fi
  done

  # Always-set directories
  for d in "requests" "specs"; do
    if [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/$d" ]]; then
      doc_add "workspace" "pass" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/$d/" "always-set directory present"
    else
      doc_add "workspace" "error" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/$d/" "always-set directory missing" \
        "mkdir -p .spectacular/$d (mechanical fix available)" "mechanical"
    fi
  done

  # config.yaml parses + has project: stanza
  if [[ -f "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" ]]; then
    # Real YAML parse via Python if available (PyYAML is stdlib-adjacent; degrade if absent)
    local yaml_ok=true
    local yaml_err=""
    if command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      # Print only the YAMLError class name + message; drop traceback noise
      local yaml_code=0
      if yaml_err=$(python3 -c '
import sys
try:
    import yaml
except ModuleNotFoundError:
    sys.exit(3)
try:
    yaml.safe_load(open(sys.argv[1]))
except yaml.YAMLError as e:
    msg = str(e).replace("\n", " ").strip()
    print(msg[:200])
    sys.exit(1)
' "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" 2>&1); then
        :
      else
        yaml_code=$?
        # PyYAML is optional: exit 3 means the parser is unavailable, so
        # degrade to the structural project: check below as documented.
        [[ $yaml_code -eq 3 ]] || yaml_ok=false
        [[ $yaml_code -eq 3 ]] && yaml_err=""
      fi
    fi
    if ! $yaml_ok; then
      doc_add "workspace" "error" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" "config.yaml is not valid YAML: ${yaml_err:-parse failed}" \
        "fix YAML syntax in config.yaml" "judgment"
    elif ! grep -q "^project:" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" 2>/dev/null; then
      doc_add "workspace" "error" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" "config.yaml missing project: stanza" \
        "rewrite config.yaml with project name/summary/kit" "judgment"
    else
      doc_add "workspace" "pass" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" "config.yaml parses + has project: stanza"
    fi

    # Schema-behind: workspace_schema older than the CLI's CURRENT_SCHEMA means
    # this workspace was scaffolded/migrated against an older layout. Advisory —
    # migrate is the fix, but staying behind isn't broken, just outdated.
    local declared_schema
    declared_schema="$(config_workspace_schema)"
    if [[ -n "$declared_schema" ]]; then
      if [[ "$declared_schema" == "$CURRENT_SCHEMA" ]]; then
        doc_add "workspace" "pass" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" "workspace_schema ${declared_schema} matches CLI (${CURRENT_SCHEMA})"
      elif schema_lt "$declared_schema" "$CURRENT_SCHEMA"; then
        doc_add "workspace" "warning" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" \
          "workspace_schema ${declared_schema} is behind CLI (expects ${CURRENT_SCHEMA})" \
          "run \`spectacular migrate\` (preview with --dry-run)" "judgment"
      else
        # Declared newer than CLI knows — the CLI is stale, not the workspace.
        doc_add "workspace" "warning" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" \
          "workspace_schema ${declared_schema} is newer than this CLI (${CURRENT_SCHEMA}) — update the CLI" \
          "run \`spectacular init --update\`" "judgment"
      fi
    fi
  fi

  # .gitignore present + includes .spectacular.local/
  local gitignore=".gitignore"
  if [[ -f "$gitignore" ]]; then
    if grep -qF ".spectacular.local/" "$gitignore"; then
      doc_add "workspace" "pass" ".gitignore" ".spectacular.local/ ignored"
    else
      doc_add "workspace" "warning" ".gitignore" "missing .spectacular.local/ entry" \
        "append .spectacular.local/ to .gitignore" "mechanical"
    fi
  else
    doc_add "workspace" "warning" ".gitignore" ".gitignore not found; .spectacular.local/ unprotected" \
      "create .gitignore with .spectacular.local/" "mechanical"
  fi

  # v0.6+ scaffold suggestion: surface optional canonical files conventionally
  # added by `coding` / `product` kits. Single info line, listing whichever are
  # missing. Silent when all three are present. These files are opt-in — no
  # error, no warning, just discoverability for projects scaffolded against
  # older kits or that initialized with --kit blank.
  local missing_v06=()
  local path
  for v06_name in PRINCIPLES ARCHITECTURE ROADMAP; do
    if [[ "$v06_name" == "ROADMAP" ]]; then
      path="$SPEC_ROADMAPS_DIR/index.md"
    else
      path="$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/${v06_name}.md"
    fi
    [[ -f "$path" ]] || missing_v06+=("$v06_name")
  done
  if (( ${#missing_v06[@]} > 0 )); then
    local v06_list with_arg
    v06_list=$(printf '%s, ' "${missing_v06[@]}" | sed 's/, $//')
    # Bash 3-compatible lowercase via tr (macOS default is bash 3.2)
    with_arg=$(printf '%s,' "${missing_v06[@]}" | sed 's/,$//' | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')
    doc_add "workspace" "info" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/" \
      "v0.6+ conventional files missing: ${v06_list} (optional)" \
      "spectacular init --with ${with_arg}" "judgment"
  fi

  # v0.9+ ROADMAP shape detection: structured roadmaps have `**Phase:**` markers
  # and `**Scope (in):**` slots. Pre-v0.9 freeform roadmaps have only `**Status:**`
  # plus loose bullet lists. Surface as info — never error.
  local roadmap="$SPEC_ROADMAPS_DIR/index.md"
  [[ -f "$roadmap" ]] || roadmap="$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/ROADMAP.md"
  if [[ -f "$roadmap" ]]; then
    if grep -q "^## v" "$roadmap" 2>/dev/null && ! grep -q "^\*\*Phase:\*\*" "$roadmap" 2>/dev/null; then
      doc_add "workspace" "info" "$roadmap" \
        "ROADMAP uses pre-v0.7.1 freeform shape — structured grill available" \
        "spectacular roadmap grill (or: re-scaffold from templates/roadmap/base.md)" "judgment"
    fi
    # v0.10+ Icebox naming: convergent dev-tool idiom; flag pre-v0.7.2 'Bucket list'
    # heading when no Icebox heading is present yet. Mechanical fix = sed rename.
    if grep -q "^## Bucket list" "$roadmap" 2>/dev/null && ! grep -q "^## Icebox" "$roadmap" 2>/dev/null; then
      doc_add "workspace" "info" "$roadmap" \
        "ROADMAP uses pre-v0.7.2 'Bucket list' section name — convergent dev-tool idiom is 'Icebox'" \
        "rename: sed -i '' 's/^## Bucket list/## Icebox/' $roadmap" "mechanical"
    fi
  fi
}

# ── area: frontmatter ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# For each canonical .md at .spectacular/ root, check it has frontmatter delimiters
# and required fields (version, updated, summary). Schema-version drift = warning.
check_frontmatter() {
  if [[ ! -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]]; then
    return
  fi

  local required_fields="version updated summary"
  shopt -s nullglob
  # Note: only scan .spectacular root, not archive/ (archive is read-only per architecture)
  for f in "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR"/*.md; do
    local base
    base=$(basename "$f")

    # Skip snapshot files (handled by snapshots area)
    if [[ "$base" =~ @v ]]; then
      continue
    fi

    # Frontmatter delimiter check
    if ! head -1 "$f" | grep -q '^---$'; then
      doc_add "frontmatter" "error" "$f" "missing frontmatter delimiter (first line must be '---')" \
        "add proper frontmatter block" "judgment"
      continue
    fi

    # Extract frontmatter block (between first two ---)
    local fm
    fm=$(awk '/^---$/ { count++; if (count == 2) exit; next } count == 1' "$f")

    for field in $required_fields; do
      if ! echo "$fm" | grep -q "^${field}:"; then
        doc_add "frontmatter" "warning" "$f" "missing required field: ${field}" \
          "add \`${field}:\` to frontmatter" "judgment"
      fi
    done

    # ISO date check on updated:
    local updated_val
    updated_val=$(echo "$fm" | awk -F': ' '/^updated:/ { print $2; exit }' | tr -d '"' | tr -d "'")
    if [[ -n "$updated_val" ]] && ! [[ "$updated_val" =~ ^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$ ]]; then
      doc_add "frontmatter" "warning" "$f" "\`updated:\` not in ISO format (got: $updated_val)" \
        "use YYYY-MM-DD format" "judgment"
    fi
  done
  shopt -u nullglob
}

# ── area: snapshots ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical layout: <store>/<DOC>/@v<N>.md (store = config_snapshots_folder,
# default _snapshots since b16; pre-b16 default was snapshots/).
# Legacy layout (pre-v1.5): .spectacular/<DOC>@v<N>.md at root.
# Checks:
#   1. Legacy root-level snapshots → warning with --fix migration path
#   2. Folder migration: old snapshots/ present while config wants _snapshots/
#   3. Version-sequence gaps in the store tree
#   4. Retention: snapshots outside the kept tiers (prunable) → info
check_snapshots() {
  if [[ ! -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]]; then
    return
  fi

  local snap_root snap_folder
  snap_root="$(snapshot_store_root)"
  snap_folder="$(config_snapshots_folder)"

  # ── 1. Legacy root-level snapshot detection (migration warning) ─────────────
  shopt -s nullglob
  local legacy=("$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR"/*@v*.md)
  shopt -u nullglob
  if [[ ${#legacy[@]} -gt 0 ]]; then
    for s in "${legacy[@]}"; do
      local b doc_prefix ver_part target
      b=$(basename "$s")
      doc_prefix="${b%@v*}"
      ver_part="@v${b#*@v}"
      target="${snap_root}/${doc_prefix}/${ver_part}"
      doc_add "snapshots" "warning" "$s" \
        "legacy root-level snapshot (layout is <store>/<DOC>/@v<N>.md)" \
        "spectacular doctor --fix snapshots  # moves to $target" \
        "mechanical"
    done
  fi

  # ── 2. Folder migration: old snapshots/ while config wants a different store ─
  if [[ "$snap_folder" != "snapshots" && -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/snapshots" && ! -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/$snap_folder" ]]; then
    doc_add "snapshots" "warning" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/snapshots/" \
      "snapshot store is at snapshots/ but config wants ${snap_folder}/ (b16 rename)" \
      "spectacular doctor --fix snapshots  # renames snapshots/ → ${snap_folder}/" \
      "mechanical"
  fi

  # ── 2b. gitignore drift: .gitignore line doesn't match snapshots.gitignore ──
  local want_gi gi_entry gi_present=0
  want_gi="$(config_snapshots_gitignore)"
  gi_entry="$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/${snap_folder}/"
  grep -qxF "$gi_entry" .gitignore 2>/dev/null && gi_present=1
  if [[ "$want_gi" == "true" && "$gi_present" -eq 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "snapshots" "warning" ".gitignore" \
      "snapshots.gitignore is true but $gi_entry is not in .gitignore" \
      "spectacular doctor --fix snapshots  # adds the ignore line" "mechanical"
  elif [[ "$want_gi" == "false" && "$gi_present" -eq 1 ]]; then
    doc_add "snapshots" "warning" ".gitignore" \
      "snapshots.gitignore is false but $gi_entry is in .gitignore" \
      "spectacular doctor --fix snapshots  # removes the ignore line" "mechanical"
  fi

  # ── 3. Gap detection (bash 3.2: no globstar — enumerate known depths) ───────
  shopt -s nullglob
  local snapshots=("$snap_root"/*/@v*.md "$snap_root"/*/*/@v*.md "$snap_root"/*/*/*/@v*.md)
  shopt -u nullglob
  # Deduplicate (the two globs overlap on direct children).
  # Note: bash 3.2 + `set -u` errors on `"${arr[@]}"` for an empty array, so
  # guard expansions with the `${arr[@]+...}` idiom (expands to nothing if empty).
  local seen="" dedup=()
  for s in ${snapshots[@]+"${snapshots[@]}"}; do
    if ! in_list "$s" "$seen"; then
      seen+="$s "
      dedup+=("$s")
    fi
  done
  snapshots=(${dedup[@]+"${dedup[@]}"})

  if [[ ${#snapshots[@]} -eq 0 && ${#legacy[@]} -eq 0 ]]; then
    return  # No snapshots is fine — many workspaces have none yet
  fi

  # Collect unique doc paths (the snapshots/<...>/ container, identifies the doc).
  # Guarded expansion (bash 3.2 + set -u): snapshots may be empty when only
  # legacy root-level snapshots exist.
  local doc_dirs=""
  for s in ${snapshots[@]+"${snapshots[@]}"}; do
    local d
    d=$(dirname "$s")
    if ! in_list "$d" "$doc_dirs"; then
      doc_dirs+="$d "
    fi
  done

  # For each doc dir, collect versions and check continuity
  for doc_dir in $doc_dirs; do
    # Derive the doc-base name (last segment of doc_dir, used for error labeling)
    local base
    base=$(basename "$doc_dir")
    local versions=""
    for s in ${snapshots[@]+"${snapshots[@]}"}; do
      [[ "$(dirname "$s")" == "$doc_dir" ]] || continue
      local b
      b=$(basename "$s")
      # Extract X.Y from @vX.Y.md
      local ver="${b#@v}"
      ver="${ver%.md}"
      versions+="$ver "
    done

    # Parse major.minor pairs, sort, look for gaps in the minor sequence within
    # each major. Heuristic: if v<M>.<N1> and v<M>.<N3> exist but v<M>.<N2> is
    # missing for any 0 < N2 < max minor, flag the gap.
    local sorted
    sorted=$(echo "$versions" | tr ' ' '\n' | sort -t. -k1n -k2n | grep -v '^$' | tr '\n' ' ')

    # Skip gap detection when the dir MIXES counter names (@vN, no dot — pre-b16
    # or version-less docs) with version-coupled names (@vX.Y). They aren't a
    # single sequence, so a "gap" between them is a false positive. Once a doc is
    # fully on either scheme the check resumes. (b16 transition guard.)
    local has_counter=0 has_dotted=0
    for v in $sorted; do
      if [[ "$v" == *.* ]]; then has_dotted=1; else has_counter=1; fi
    done
    if (( has_counter && has_dotted )); then
      doc_add "snapshots" "info" "${doc_dir}/@v*.md" \
        "$(echo "$sorted" | wc -w | tr -d ' ') snapshot(s) for $base (mixed counter + version names — gap check skipped)"
      continue
    fi

    # Build minor-version list per major
    local prev_major="" prev_minor=""
    for v in $sorted; do
      local major="${v%.*}"
      local minor="${v#*.}"
      if [[ "$major" == "$prev_major" ]]; then
        local expected=$((prev_minor + 1))
        while [[ $expected -lt $minor ]]; do
          local missing="${major}.${expected}"
          doc_add "snapshots" "warning" "${doc_dir}/@v${missing}.md" \
            "version-sequence gap (have v${prev_major}.${prev_minor} and v${major}.${minor})" \
            "backfill from git log if possible, or document the skip in DECISIONS.md" \
            "judgment"
          expected=$((expected + 1))
        done
      fi
      prev_major="$major"
      prev_minor="$minor"
    done

    if [[ -z "$sorted" ]]; then continue; fi
    doc_add "snapshots" "info" "${doc_dir}/@v*.md" \
      "$(echo "$sorted" | wc -w | tr -d ' ') snapshot(s) found for $base"

    # ── 4. Retention: count snapshots outside the kept tiers (prunable) ───────
    local keep period kept=" " all_count=0 prunable=0
    keep="$(config_snapshots_keep)"; period="$(config_snapshots_period)"
    local kb
    while IFS= read -r kb; do [[ -n "$kb" ]] && kept+="$kb "; done < <(snapshot_retained_set "$doc_dir" "$keep" "$period")
    shopt -s nullglob
    local sf
    for sf in "$doc_dir"/@v*; do
      all_count=$(( all_count + 1 ))
      [[ "$kept" == *" $(basename "$sf") "* ]] || prunable=$(( prunable + 1 ))
    done
    shopt -u nullglob
    if (( prunable > 0 )); then
      doc_add "snapshots" "info" "${doc_dir}/@v*.md" \
        "$prunable of $all_count snapshot(s) outside retention (keep $keep, $period) for $base" \
        "spectacular snapshot prune       # preview, then --apply" \
        "judgment"
    fi
  done
}

# ── area: links ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Walk every canonical .md, extract `related:` frontmatter entries, verify each
# target exists (resolved relative to the file's location).
check_links() {
  if [[ ! -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]]; then return; fi

  # Root-aware target resolution (v1.16.0+):
  # - Bare slug (no '/', no '.md') → resolve as request slug: requests/<slug>/PLAN.md
  #   or archive/<slug>/PLAN.md (archived = satisfied)
  # - Root doc name (PRD.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, etc.) → resolve at .spectacular/
  # - Anything with '/' → resolve relative to the file's own dir (legacy behaviour)
  local -a _root_docs=(PRD.md ARCHITECTURE.md ROADMAP.md PRINCIPLES.md AGENTS.md
                       STACK.md DECISIONS.md SPEC.md PERSONAS.md POLICY.md)

  _cl_resolve_target() {
    local target="$1" file="$2"
    # Bare slug: no slash, not ending in .md
    if [[ "$target" != */* ]] && [[ "$target" != *.md ]]; then
      # depends-on:/blocks: are always slugs; handle via _cl_check_slug below
      echo "slug:$target"
      return
    fi
    # Root doc (just a filename, matches known root doc names)
    for _rd in "${_root_docs[@]}"; do
      if [[ "$target" == "$_rd" ]]; then
        echo "file:.spectacular/$target"
        return
      fi
    done
    # Relative path → resolve from file's dir
    echo "file:$(dirname "$file")/$target"
  }

  _cl_check_slug() {
    local slug="$1" file="$2" field="$3"
    if [[ -f "$SPEC_REQUESTS_DIR/$slug/PLAN.md" ]]; then
      : # active request — valid
    elif [[ -f "$SPEC_ARCHIVE_DIR/$slug/PLAN.md" ]]; then
      : # archived = satisfied — valid, not a warning
    else
      doc_add "links" "warning" "$file" \
        "$field: slug '$slug' not found in requests/ or archive/" \
        "remove the stale link or create the request" \
        "judgment"
    fi
  }

  shopt -s nullglob
  while IFS= read -r f; do
    [[ -f "$f" ]] || continue
    if [[ "$(basename "$f")" =~ @v ]]; then continue; fi
    if [[ "$f" == *"$SPEC_ARCHIVE_DIR/"* ]]; then continue; fi

    local in_fm=false cur_field=""
    while IFS= read -r line; do
      if [[ "$line" == "---" ]]; then
        if $in_fm; then break; else in_fm=true; continue; fi
      fi
      $in_fm || continue

      # Detect which list field we're in (related:, depends-on:, blocks:, conflicts-with:)
      if [[ "$line" =~ ^related: ]];    then cur_field="related";    continue; fi
      if [[ "$line" =~ ^depends-on: ]]; then cur_field="depends-on"; continue; fi
      if [[ "$line" =~ ^blocks: ]];     then cur_field="blocks";     continue; fi
      if [[ "$line" =~ ^conflicts-with: ]]; then cur_field="conflicts-with"; continue; fi
      # Exit current field on next top-level key
      if [[ -n "$cur_field" ]] && [[ "$line" =~ ^[a-zA-Z] ]]; then cur_field=""; fi

      if [[ -n "$cur_field" ]] && [[ "$line" =~ ^[[:space:]]+-[[:space:]]+(.+)$ ]]; then
        local target="${BASH_REMATCH[1]}"
        target="${target%%#*}"
        target="${target%\"}"; target="${target#\"}"
        target="${target%\'}"; target="${target#\'}"
        target="$(echo "$target" | xargs)"
        [[ -z "$target" ]] && continue

        if [[ "$cur_field" == "depends-on" ]] || [[ "$cur_field" == "blocks" ]] || [[ "$cur_field" == "conflicts-with" ]]; then
          # These fields only accept slugs
          _cl_check_slug "$target" "$f" "$cur_field"
        else
          # related: — root-aware resolution
          local resolved_spec
          resolved_spec=$(_cl_resolve_target "$target" "$f")
          case "$resolved_spec" in
            slug:*)
              _cl_check_slug "${resolved_spec#slug:}" "$f" "related"
              ;;
            file:*)
              local resolved="${resolved_spec#file:}"
              if [[ ! -e "$resolved" ]]; then
                doc_add "links" "warning" "$f" \
                  "related: target '$target' does not exist (resolved: $resolved)" \
                  "remove the stale link or fix the target" \
                  "judgment"
              fi
              ;;
          esac
        fi
      fi
    done < "$f"
  done < <(find "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" -type f -name "*.md")
  shopt -u nullglob

  if ! echo "$DOC_FINDINGS" | grep -q "^links|warning"; then
    doc_add "links" "pass" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/" "all related:/depends-on:/blocks:/conflicts-with: targets resolve"
  fi
}

# PLAN/TASKS canonical structure enforcement (schema-enforcement change).
# Appends doc_add findings and bumps the global _STRUCT_ISSUES counter. Called
# per-request from check_lifecycle, which only iterates .spectacular/requests/
# (never archive/), so this errors on active requests and skips archive by
# construction. Required PLAN sections, unnumbered + in order:
#   Goal, Constraints, Milestones, Tasks, Dependencies, Validation, Deliverables
# (extra sections allowed between them). TASKS must have ≥1 ### M heading and no
# malformed checkbox. The legacy numbered form (## 1. Goal) is a fixable error.
_STRUCT_ISSUES=0
_PLAN_REQUIRED_SECTIONS="Goal Constraints Milestones Tasks Dependencies Validation Deliverables"
_check_request_structure() {
  local slug="$1" plan="$2" tasks="$3"

  if [[ -f "$plan" ]]; then
    # Detect legacy numbered headings (## 1. Goal …) — fixable.
    if grep -qE '^## [0-9]+\. (Goal|Constraints|Milestones|Tasks|Dependencies|Validation|Deliverables)' "$plan"; then
      doc_add "lifecycle" "error" "$plan" \
        "request '$slug': PLAN uses legacy numbered section headings (## 1. Goal …)" \
        "run \`spectacular doctor --fix\` to rewrite them to the unnumbered canonical form (## Goal …)" \
        "mechanical"
      _STRUCT_ISSUES=$((_STRUCT_ISSUES + 1))
    fi

    # Required sections present + in order. Collect the canonical headings that
    # appear (accepting both unnumbered and legacy numbered), in file order.
    local seen order_ok=1 prev_idx=0 missing=""
    local sec idx line
    # Build the ordered list of required headings found.
    local found_order
    found_order=$(grep -oE '^## ([0-9]+\. )?(Goal|Constraints|Milestones|Tasks|Dependencies|Validation|Deliverables)$' "$plan" 2>/dev/null \
      | sed -E 's/^## ([0-9]+\. )?//')
    for sec in $_PLAN_REQUIRED_SECTIONS; do
      if ! echo "$found_order" | grep -qx "$sec"; then
        missing="$missing $sec"
      fi
    done
    if [[ -n "$missing" ]]; then
      doc_add "lifecycle" "error" "$plan" \
        "request '$slug': PLAN missing required section(s):$missing" \
        "add the missing ## <Section> heading(s) — canonical order: Goal, Constraints, Milestones, Tasks, Dependencies, Validation, Deliverables" \
        "judgment"
      _STRUCT_ISSUES=$((_STRUCT_ISSUES + 1))
    else
      # All present — verify order matches the canonical sequence.
      local expected="Goal Constraints Milestones Tasks Dependencies Validation Deliverables"
      local got
      got=$(echo "$found_order" | tr '\n' ' ' | sed -E 's/ +/ /g; s/^ //; s/ $//')
      if [[ "$got" != "$expected" ]]; then
        doc_add "lifecycle" "error" "$plan" \
          "request '$slug': PLAN sections out of canonical order (got: $got)" \
          "reorder to: Goal, Constraints, Milestones, Tasks, Dependencies, Validation, Deliverables" \
          "judgment"
        _STRUCT_ISSUES=$((_STRUCT_ISSUES + 1))
      fi
    fi
  fi

  if [[ -f "$tasks" ]]; then
    # Must group by ### M<N> milestones.
    if ! grep -qE '^### M[0-9]+' "$tasks"; then
      doc_add "lifecycle" "error" "$tasks" \
        "request '$slug': TASKS has no '### M<N>' milestone headings" \
        "group tasks under '### M1 — <name>' headings so status can read the current milestone" \
        "judgment"
      _STRUCT_ISSUES=$((_STRUCT_ISSUES + 1))
    fi
    # Malformed checkbox states (typos). Valid: [ ] [x] [~]. Flag anything else
    # inside a leading "- [.]"-shaped bullet, flush-left or indented.
    if grep -qE '^[[:space:]]*- \[[^ x~]\]' "$tasks"; then
      local bad
      bad=$(grep -oE '^[[:space:]]*- \[[^ x~]\]' "$tasks" | sort -u | tr '\n' ' ' | xargs)
      doc_add "lifecycle" "error" "$tasks" \
        "request '$slug': TASKS has malformed checkbox state(s): $bad" \
        "use only '- [ ]' (open), '- [x]' (done), or '- [~]' (deferred)" \
        "judgment"
      _STRUCT_ISSUES=$((_STRUCT_ISSUES + 1))
    fi
  fi
}

# ── area: lifecycle ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# For each request, check status frontmatter against required artifacts.
check_lifecycle() {
  if [[ ! -d "$SPEC_REQUESTS_DIR" ]]; then return; fi

  shopt -s nullglob
  local request_dirs=("$SPEC_REQUESTS_DIR"/*/)
  shopt -u nullglob

  if [[ ${#request_dirs[@]} -eq 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "lifecycle" "info" "$SPEC_REQUESTS_DIR/" "no requests yet"
    return
  fi

  local issues=0
  for d in "${request_dirs[@]}"; do
    local plan="$d/PLAN.md"
    local slug
    slug=$(basename "$d")

    if [[ ! -f "$plan" ]]; then
      doc_add "lifecycle" "warning" "$plan" "request '$slug' has no PLAN.md" "" "judgment"
      issues=$((issues + 1))
      continue
    fi

    local status
    status=$(awk -F': ' '/^---$/{c++; next} c==1 && /^status:/ { print $2; exit }' "$plan" | tr -d '"' | tr -d "'" | xargs)

    local source_spec source_type source_ref sensitivity provenance_missing="" provenance_key
    source_spec=$(fm_get "$plan" contract); [[ -n "$source_spec" ]] || source_spec=$(fm_get "$plan" source_spec)
    source_type=$(fm_get "$plan" source_type); source_ref=$(fm_get "$plan" source_ref)
    sensitivity=$(fm_get "$plan" sensitivity)
    if [[ -n "$source_type" || -n "$source_ref" ]]; then
      case "$source_type" in issue|spec|goal) ;; *)
        doc_add "lifecycle" "error" "$plan" "request '$slug' has invalid source_type '${source_type:-missing}'" \
          "use issue, spec, or goal and preserve the canonical source_ref" "mechanical"
        issues=$((issues + 1)) ;;
      esac
      if [[ -z "$source_ref" ]]; then
        doc_add "lifecycle" "error" "$plan" "request '$slug' has source_type $source_type but no source_ref" \
          "record the canonical source identity without copying its body" "mechanical"
        issues=$((issues + 1))
      fi
      if [[ "$source_type" == issue && -n "$source_ref" && ! "$source_ref" =~ ^[^/[:space:]]+/[^#[:space:]]+#[0-9]+$ ]]; then
        doc_add "lifecycle" "error" "$plan" "request '$slug' has malformed Issue source_ref '$source_ref'" \
          "use canonical owner/repo#N identity" "mechanical"
        issues=$((issues + 1))
      fi
      if [[ "$source_type" == issue || "$source_type" == goal ]]; then
        case "$sensitivity" in normal|protected) ;; *)
          doc_add "lifecycle" "error" "$plan" "request '$slug' has no valid sensitivity classification" \
            "record sensitivity: normal|protected; protected work cannot use the ordinary PR path" "mechanical"
          issues=$((issues + 1)) ;;
        esac
      fi
      if [[ "$status" =~ ^(active|review|verified)$ ]]; then
        for provenance_key in activated_at activated_by activated_against; do
          [[ -n "$(fm_get "$plan" "$provenance_key")" ]] || provenance_missing="${provenance_missing:+$provenance_missing, }$provenance_key"
        done
      fi
    fi
    if [[ -n "$provenance_missing" ]]; then
      doc_add "lifecycle" "error" "$plan" \
        "request '$slug' has incomplete source/activation provenance: $provenance_missing" \
        "record the contract identity and activation actor/date/Git baseline" \
        "mechanical"
      issues=$((issues + 1))
    fi

    # Optional coordination metadata is deliberately additive: legacy requests
    # remain valid when it is absent, but a supplied value must be usable Git
    # evidence rather than a free-form label.
    local declared_branch declared_base
    declared_branch=$(fm_get "$plan" branch); declared_base=$(fm_get "$plan" base)
    if [[ -n "$declared_branch" && ! "$declared_branch" =~ ^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._/-]*$ ]]; then
      doc_add "lifecycle" "warning" "$plan" "request '$slug' has malformed optional branch: '$declared_branch'" \
        "use a Git branch name, or omit branch: when unknown" "judgment"
      issues=$((issues + 1))
    fi
    if [[ -n "$declared_base" && ! "$declared_base" =~ ^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._/-]*$ ]]; then
      doc_add "lifecycle" "warning" "$plan" "request '$slug' has malformed optional base: '$declared_base'" \
        "use a Git base branch name, or omit base: when unknown" "judgment"
      issues=$((issues + 1))
    fi

    local docs_impact; docs_impact=$(fm_get "$plan" docs_impact)
    if [[ -n "$docs_impact" && "$status" =~ ^(active|review|verified)$ ]] && ! _request_docs_impact_closed "$plan"; then
      doc_add "lifecycle" "warning" "$plan" "request '$slug' has unresolved docs impact ($docs_impact)" \
        "record none+reason or required+evidence before verification/archive" "judgment"
      issues=$((issues + 1))
    fi

    case "$status" in
      active)
        if [[ ! -f "$d/SESSION.md" ]]; then
          doc_add "lifecycle" "warning" "$d" "request '$slug' active without SESSION.md" \
            "create SESSION.md or move status back to planned" "judgment"
          issues=$((issues + 1))
        fi
        ;;
      review|verified)
        # Must have at least one verification artifact:
        # VERIFY.md OR TASKS.md with ### Verification section OR PLAN.md with ## Validation
        local has_verify=false
        if [[ -f "$d/VERIFY.md" ]]; then
          has_verify=true
          # When status=verified, VERIFY.md must have zero unchecked items
          if [[ "$status" == "verified" ]] && grep -qE '^- \[ \]' "$d/VERIFY.md"; then
            doc_add "lifecycle" "error" "$d/VERIFY.md" \
              "request '$slug' is verified but VERIFY.md has unchecked items" \
              "complete remaining items or move status back to review" \
              "judgment"
            issues=$((issues + 1))
          fi
        fi
        if ! $has_verify; then
          local has_tasks_verif=false
          [[ -f "$d/TASKS.md" ]] && grep -qE "^### Verification|^## Verification" "$d/TASKS.md" && has_tasks_verif=true
          local has_plan_valid=false
          # Per [[verification]], PLAN's validation may live under several heading names:
          # "Validation", "Success criteria", "Goals & success criteria", or "Acceptance"
          grep -qE "^## .*[Vv]alidation|^## .*[Ss]uccess criteria|^## .*[Aa]cceptance" "$plan" && has_plan_valid=true
          if ! $has_tasks_verif && ! $has_plan_valid; then
            doc_add "lifecycle" "error" "$d" \
              "request '$slug' is $status without any verification artifact (VERIFY.md / TASKS Verification / PLAN Validation)" \
              "add one of: VERIFY.md (2-of-6 rule), TASKS § Verification, or PLAN § Validation/Success criteria" \
              "judgment"
            issues=$((issues + 1))
          fi
        fi

        # Evidence freshness (b31): [manual]/[observe] passed rows must carry an
        # against: stamp; pending-reverify rows mean evidence went stale. Presence
        # checks only — staleness itself is a judgment flip, never a git heuristic.
        if [[ -f "$d/VERIFY-LOG.md" ]]; then
          local ev_total ev_stamped ev_unstamped ev_pending
          ev_total=$(grep -cE '^- ✓ \[(manual|observe)\]' "$d/VERIFY-LOG.md" 2>/dev/null || true)
          ev_stamped=$(grep -cE '^- ✓ \[(manual|observe)\].*against:' "$d/VERIFY-LOG.md" 2>/dev/null || true)
          ev_unstamped=$(( ${ev_total:-0} - ${ev_stamped:-0} ))
          if (( ev_unstamped > 0 )); then
            doc_add "lifecycle" "warning" "$d/VERIFY-LOG.md" \
              "request '$slug' has $ev_unstamped manual/observe evidence row(s) without an against: stamp" \
              "re-record with 'against: <commit/build> · <identity>' so evidence can be told from stale evidence" \
              "judgment"
            issues=$((issues + 1))
          fi
          ev_pending=$(grep -c 'pending-reverify' "$d/VERIFY-LOG.md" 2>/dev/null || true)
          if (( ${ev_pending:-0} > 0 )); then
            doc_add "lifecycle" "warning" "$d/VERIFY-LOG.md" \
              "request '$slug' is $status with $ev_pending pending-reverify evidence row(s) — stale evidence not re-proven" \
              "re-perform the check(s) against the current build, record fresh stamped rows" \
              "judgment"
            issues=$((issues + 1))
          fi
        fi

        # Stale verified — info only
        if [[ "$status" == "verified" ]]; then
          if { [[ ! -f "$d/VERIFY-LOG.md" ]] || ! grep -Eq '✅|^result:[[:space:]]*pass([[:space:]]|$)|\*\*Outcome:\*\*[[:space:]]*verified' "$d/VERIFY-LOG.md"; } \
             && [[ -z "$(fm_get "$plan" verification_override)" ]]; then
            doc_add "lifecycle" "warning" "$plan" \
              "request '$slug' is verified without passing VERIFY-LOG evidence or a recorded verification override" \
              "run /spectacular verify against the current build, or record an exceptional --override verify --reason" \
              "mechanical"
            issues=$((issues + 1))
          fi
          local updated
          updated=$(awk -F': ' '/^---$/{c++; next} c==1 && /^updated:/ { print $2; exit }' "$plan" | tr -d '"' | tr -d "'" | xargs)
          if [[ -n "$updated" ]]; then
            local age_days
            age_days=$(( ( $(date +%s) - $(date -j -f "%Y-%m-%d" "$updated" +%s 2>/dev/null || echo 0) ) / 86400 ))
            if [[ $age_days -gt 7 && $age_days -lt 99999 ]]; then
              doc_add "lifecycle" "info" "$d" \
                "request '$slug' verified $age_days days ago — archive candidate" \
                "run \`spectacular archive $slug\`" \
                "judgment"
            fi
          fi
        fi
        ;;
      planned)
        : # No verification artifact required for planned
        ;;
      "")
        doc_add "lifecycle" "warning" "$plan" "request '$slug' has no status: field" "" "judgment"
        issues=$((issues + 1))
        ;;
    esac

    # Milestone (M<N>) label alignment across TASKS.md / PLAN §3 / PLAN §6.
    # Advisory only: the chain (task row -> milestone block -> plan section -> validation)
    # should still be walkable by number+name even when labels drift, so mismatches are a
    # warning to fix, never a blocker. Two checks:
    #   1. off-prefix heading (e.g. "### G1 —" instead of "### M1 —") — a real drift risk,
    #      since M is the project-wide standard for milestones (D<N>=decisions, F<N>=fixes,
    #      b<N>=roadmap builds all follow the same one-letter-per-namespace convention).
    #   2. number mismatch — but only reported after a name-based fallback match fails, since
    #      the milestone NAME (not the M<N> token) is the real stable link between files.
    local tasks="$d/TASKS.md"
    if [[ -f "$tasks" ]]; then
      # Off-standard milestone prefix: any "### <Letter><N> —" heading where Letter != M.
      local off_prefix
      off_prefix=$(grep -oE '^#{2,3} [A-Za-z][0-9]+ —' "$tasks" 2>/dev/null | grep -vE '^#{2,3} M[0-9]+ —' | sed -E 's/^#+ //; s/ —$//' | sort -u) || true
      if [[ -n "$off_prefix" ]]; then
        doc_add "lifecycle" "warning" "$tasks" \
          "request '$slug': TASKS.md uses non-standard milestone prefix(es): $(echo "$off_prefix" | xargs)" \
          "milestones use 'M<N>' project-wide (mirrors D<N>=decisions, F<N>=fixes, b<N>=roadmap builds) — rename to M<N> so the chain stays greppable by convention, not just by name" \
          "judgment"
        issues=$((issues + 1))
      fi

      # Milestone/Validation sections use UNNUMBERED headings (## Milestones,
      # ## Validation) since the schema-enforcement change; fall back to the
      # legacy numbered form (## 3. Milestones) for not-yet-converted requests.
      # Use `sed -nE` (ERE): BSD sed does not support `\?` in BRE, so the
      # optional numbered-prefix group must be `(3\. )?` under -E.
      local ms_tasks ms_plan3 ms_plan6
      ms_tasks=$(grep -oE '^#{2,3} M[0-9]+ —' "$tasks" 2>/dev/null | grep -oE 'M[0-9]+' | sort -u) || true
      ms_plan3=$(sed -nE '/^## (3\. )?Milestones/,/^## (4\. )?Tasks/p' "$plan" 2>/dev/null | grep -oE '^- M[0-9]+ —' | grep -oE 'M[0-9]+' | sort -u) || true
      ms_plan6=$(sed -nE '/^## (6\. )?Validation/,/^## (7\. )?Deliverables/p' "$plan" 2>/dev/null | grep -oE '^- M[0-9]+ —' | grep -oE 'M[0-9]+' | sort -u) || true

      # Name-based fallback: first few words after the "M<N> — " marker (or any "<ID> — " marker),
      # lowercased, so a renamed/relettered heading can still match by what it's actually called.
      local names_tasks names_plan3
      names_tasks=$(grep -oE '^#{2,3} [A-Za-z][0-9]+ — [A-Za-z0-9 ]+' "$tasks" 2>/dev/null | sed -E 's/^#+ [A-Za-z][0-9]+ — //' | awk '{print tolower($1" "$2)}' | sort -u) || true
      names_plan3=$(sed -nE '/^## (3\. )?Milestones/,/^## (4\. )?Tasks/p' "$plan" 2>/dev/null | grep -oE '^- [A-Za-z][0-9]+ — [A-Za-z0-9 ]+' | sed -E 's/^- [A-Za-z][0-9]+ — //' | awk '{print tolower($1" "$2)}' | sort -u) || true
      local names_match=1
      [[ "$names_tasks" == "$names_plan3" ]] && names_match=0

      if [[ -n "$ms_tasks" && -n "$ms_plan3" && "$ms_tasks" != "$ms_plan3" && $names_match -ne 0 ]]; then
        doc_add "lifecycle" "warning" "$tasks" \
          "request '$slug': milestone labels differ between TASKS.md ($(echo "$ms_tasks" | xargs)) and PLAN Milestones ($(echo "$ms_plan3" | xargs)), and names don't line up either" \
          "renumber so M<N> matches 1:1 across TASKS.md and PLAN Milestones — a Builder/agent walking the chain by number will otherwise mismatch milestones" \
          "judgment"
        issues=$((issues + 1))
      fi
      if [[ -n "$ms_plan3" && -n "$ms_plan6" && "$ms_plan3" != "$ms_plan6" ]]; then
        doc_add "lifecycle" "warning" "$plan" \
          "request '$slug': milestone labels differ between PLAN Milestones ($(echo "$ms_plan3" | xargs)) and Validation ($(echo "$ms_plan6" | xargs))" \
          "renumber so M<N> matches 1:1 across Milestones and Validation — validation criteria won't map cleanly to their milestone otherwise" \
          "judgment"
        issues=$((issues + 1))
      fi
    fi

    # ── PLAN/TASKS structure enforcement (schema-enforcement change) ──────────
    # Errors on ACTIVE requests only; archive/ is never reached (this loop only
    # iterates .spectacular/requests/). The 7 required PLAN sections must appear
    # unnumbered and in order; TASKS must group by ### M and use valid checkbox
    # syntax. --fix rewrites the numbered legacy form.
    _STRUCT_ISSUES=0
    _check_request_structure "$slug" "$plan" "$d/TASKS.md"
    issues=$((issues + _STRUCT_ISSUES))
  done

  if [[ $issues -eq 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "lifecycle" "pass" "$SPEC_REQUESTS_DIR/" "all requests have valid lifecycle state"
  fi
}

# ── area: kits ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
check_kits() {
  local agents_dir
  agents_dir="$(agents_skill_dir)"
  local kits_dir="$agents_dir/templates/prd/kits"

  if [[ ! -d "$kits_dir" ]]; then
    doc_add "kits" "warning" "$kits_dir" "bundled kits directory missing" \
      "re-install skill via \`spectacular init --update\`" "judgment"
    return
  fi

  shopt -s nullglob
  local kit_files=("$kits_dir"/*.md)
  shopt -u nullglob

  local ok=0 bad=0
  for kit in "${kit_files[@]}"; do
    local name
    name=$(basename "$kit" .md)
    # Frontmatter present?
    if ! head -1 "$kit" | grep -q '^---$'; then
      doc_add "kits" "error" "$kit" "kit '$name' has no frontmatter" \
        "fix kit frontmatter or re-install skill" "judgment"
      bad=$((bad + 1))
      continue
    fi
    # extends: prd (only allowed value in v1)
    local extends_val
    extends_val=$(awk -F': ' '/^---$/{c++; next} c==1 && /^extends:/ { print $2; exit }' "$kit" | xargs)
    if [[ -n "$extends_val" && "$extends_val" != "prd" ]]; then
      doc_add "kits" "error" "$kit" "kit '$name' extends '$extends_val' (only 'prd' allowed in v1)" \
        "change to extends: prd or remove kit" "judgment"
      bad=$((bad + 1))
      continue
    fi
    # triggers-docs entries match KNOWN_DOCS
    local triggers
    triggers=$(kit_triggers "$name" always)
    triggers+=" $(kit_triggers "$name" suggested)"
    local kit_ok=true
    for doc in $triggers; do
      [[ -z "$doc" ]] && continue
      if ! in_list "$doc" "$KNOWN_DOCS"; then
        doc_add "kits" "warning" "$kit" "kit '$name' triggers-docs references unknown doc ID: '$doc'" \
          "remove or rename to a known doc ID: $KNOWN_DOCS" "judgment"
        kit_ok=false
      fi
    done
    if $kit_ok; then ok=$((ok + 1)); else bad=$((bad + 1)); fi
  done

  # Project-local kits override
  local local_kits="$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/templates/prd/kits"
  if [[ -d "$local_kits" ]]; then
    shopt -s nullglob
    local local_files=("$local_kits"/*.md)
    shopt -u nullglob
    if [[ ${#local_files[@]} -gt 0 ]]; then
      doc_add "kits" "info" "$local_kits" "${#local_files[@]} project-local kit override(s) found"
    fi
  fi

  # PRD kit identity check
  if [[ -f "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/PRD.md" ]]; then
    local prd_kit
    prd_kit=$(awk -F': ' '/^---$/{c++; next} c==1 && /^kit:/ { print $2; exit }' "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/PRD.md" | xargs)
    if [[ -n "$prd_kit" ]]; then
      if [[ -f "$kits_dir/$prd_kit.md" ]] || [[ -f "$local_kits/$prd_kit.md" ]]; then
        doc_add "kits" "pass" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/PRD.md" "declared kit '$prd_kit' is resolvable"
      else
        doc_add "kits" "error" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/PRD.md" "declares kit '$prd_kit' but no matching kit file found" \
          "install missing kit or change PRD's kit: field" "judgment"
      fi
    fi
  fi

  if [[ $bad -eq 0 && $ok -gt 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "kits" "pass" "$kits_dir" "$ok bundled kits parse cleanly"
  fi

  # Migration chain validation (v0.6.2+)
  # Validates skill-internal registry under references/migrations/.
  # See: skills/spectacular/references/migrations-contract.md § Chain validation
  local mig_dir
  if mig_dir="$(migrations_dir 2>/dev/null)"; then
    check_migration_chain "$mig_dir"
  fi
}

# Validate the migration registry chain. Called from check_kits.
# Reports gaps, duplicates, broken apply-fn references, and id/filename drift.
check_migration_chain() {
  local mig_dir="$1"
  shopt -s nullglob
  local files=("$mig_dir"/v*.md)
  shopt -u nullglob

  if [[ ${#files[@]} -eq 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "kits" "info" "$mig_dir" "no migrations registered (registry is empty)"
    return 0
  fi

  # Build a sorted list of (from, to, id, mech, apply-fn, filename, path)
  local -a entries=()
  local f
  for f in "${files[@]}"; do
    local basename id from to mech applyfn rev
    basename=$(basename "$f" .md)
    id="$(migration_field "$f" "id")"
    from="$(migration_field "$f" "from")"
    to="$(migration_field "$f" "to")"
    mech="$(migration_field "$f" "mechanical")"
    applyfn="$(migration_field "$f" "apply-fn")"
    rev="$(migration_field "$f" "reversible")"

    # id must match filename
    if [[ "$id" != "$basename" ]]; then
      doc_add "kits" "warning" "$f" "migration id '$id' does not match filename '$basename'" \
        "rename file or update id: field" "judgment"
    fi
    # Required fields
    if [[ -z "$from" || -z "$to" ]]; then
      doc_add "kits" "error" "$f" "migration missing required from: or to: field" \
        "add from + to in frontmatter" "judgment"
      continue
    fi
    # Mechanical → apply-fn required + must be a defined bash function
    if [[ "$mech" == "true" ]]; then
      if [[ -z "$applyfn" ]]; then
        doc_add "kits" "error" "$f" "mechanical: true but apply-fn is empty" \
          "add apply-fn: <bash function name> or set mechanical: false" "judgment"
      elif ! declare -F "$applyfn" >/dev/null; then
        doc_add "kits" "error" "$f" "apply-fn '$applyfn' is not defined in cli/spectacular" \
          "define migration_apply_<id>() in cli/spectacular or fix apply-fn field" "judgment"
      fi
    fi
    # Reversible → reverse function must exist if declared
    if [[ "$rev" == "true" ]]; then
      local revfn="migration_revert_${id//-/_}"
      if ! declare -F "$revfn" >/dev/null; then
        doc_add "kits" "warning" "$f" "reversible: true but no reverse function '$revfn' defined" \
          "either define $revfn() or set reversible: false" "judgment"
      fi
    fi
    entries+=("${from}|${to}|${id}")
  done

  # Sort entries by from-version
  IFS=$'\n' read -r -d '' -a entries < <(printf '%s\n' "${entries[@]}" | sort -t'|' -V -k1,1; printf '\0')

  # Chain integrity: every from: must be either "0.4" (baseline) or match a previous to:.
  # Bash 3.2 compat: indexed-array tracking, linear search via in_list helper.
  local seen_to="0.4"          # space-separated list of reachable schema versions
  local seen_edges=""          # space-separated list of "from->to" pairs already seen
  local entry
  for entry in "${entries[@]}"; do
    IFS='|' read -r from to id <<< "$entry"
    local edge_key="${from}->${to}"
    if in_list "$edge_key" "$seen_edges"; then
      doc_add "kits" "error" "$mig_dir" "duplicate migration edge: ${edge_key} (multiple migrations declare from=${from} to=${to})" \
        "remove or merge duplicate migrations" "judgment"
    else
      seen_edges="$seen_edges $edge_key"
    fi
    if ! in_list "$from" "$seen_to"; then
      doc_add "kits" "error" "$mig_dir" "migration '${id}' has from: ${from} but no previous migration targets that version (chain gap)" \
        "add a migration whose to: is ${from}, or correct from: to a reachable version" "judgment"
    fi
    seen_to="$seen_to $to"
  done

  # Summary line on clean chain
  local chain_count=${#entries[@]}
  if [[ $chain_count -gt 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "kits" "pass" "$mig_dir" "migration chain validates (${chain_count} entries)"
  fi
}

# check_conventions — validates the active convention pack and (when mode=enforce)
# flags drift between project state and the pack's declared rules.
# Active only when .spectacular/config.yaml declares convention_pack:.
check_conventions() {
  local pack_src_name pack_mode
  pack_src_name="$(config_pack_source 2>/dev/null)"

  if [[ -z "$pack_src_name" ]]; then
    doc_add "conventions" "info" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" "no convention_pack declared — skipped"
    return
  fi

  pack_mode="$(config_pack_mode)"

  # Detect unknown-mode drift: raw value present but doesn't match allow-list.
  # config_pack_mode silently fell back to suggest; surface the original here
  # so the user knows their value was ignored.
  local pack_mode_raw
  pack_mode_raw="$(config_pack_mode_raw)"
  if [[ -n "$pack_mode_raw" ]]; then
    case "$pack_mode_raw" in
      suggest|scaffold|enforce) ;;
      *)
        doc_add "conventions" "info" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" \
          "unknown convention_pack.mode '$pack_mode_raw' (valid: suggest / scaffold / enforce) — falling back to 'suggest'" \
          "set mode to one of: suggest, scaffold, enforce" "judgment"
        ;;
    esac
  fi

  local pack_resolved
  if ! pack_resolved="$(pack_resolve "$pack_src_name")"; then
    doc_add "conventions" "error" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" \
      "convention_pack source '$pack_src_name' not found in any scope" \
      "run 'spectacular pack install $pack_src_name' or change source in config.yaml" "judgment"
    return
  fi

  doc_add "conventions" "pass" "$pack_resolved" "active pack '$pack_src_name' ($pack_mode) resolves to $(pack_scope_of "$pack_resolved")"

  # In suggest mode, doctor only reports the pack is active; no drift checks
  if [[ "$pack_mode" == "suggest" ]]; then
    doc_add "conventions" "info" "$pack_resolved" "mode=suggest — drift checks are disabled (use scaffold or enforce)"
    return
  fi

  # In scaffold/enforce modes, check gitignore alignment
  local gitignore=".gitignore"
  if [[ ! -f "$gitignore" ]]; then
    doc_add "conventions" "warning" ".gitignore" "pack '$pack_src_name' declares gitignore.always-add but .gitignore is missing" \
      "create .gitignore (or run 'spectacular init' to scaffold)" "mechanical"
    return
  fi

  local missing=0 expected=0
  while IFS= read -r entry; do
    [[ -z "$entry" ]] && continue
    expected=$((expected + 1))
    if ! grep -qF -- "$entry" "$gitignore"; then
      local sev="warning"
      [[ "$pack_mode" == "enforce" ]] && sev="error"
      doc_add "conventions" "$sev" ".gitignore" \
        "pack '$pack_src_name' requires gitignore entry: '$entry' (missing)" \
        "append to .gitignore (or run 'spectacular init' to re-apply pack)" "mechanical"
      missing=$((missing + 1))
    fi
  done < <(pack_gitignore_always_add "$pack_resolved")

  if [[ $expected -gt 0 && $missing -eq 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "conventions" "pass" ".gitignore" "all $expected required gitignore entries from pack '$pack_src_name' present"
  fi
}

# ── area: specs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Validate the system-spec surface: SPEC.md index + specs/ dir + legacy current/ migration.
# Per-capability files under specs/<capability>/SPEC.md are optional (only for complex work).
check_specs() {
  [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]] || return 0

  local spec_file="$SPEC_SPECS_DIR/index.md"
  local specs_dir="$SPEC_SPECS_DIR"
  local legacy_dir="$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/current"

  # Conflict: both current/ and specs/ present → manual merge required
  if [[ -d "$legacy_dir" && -d "$specs_dir" ]]; then
    doc_add "specs" "error" "$legacy_dir" \
      "both .spectacular/current/ and .spectacular/specs/ exist — manual merge required (no auto-fix)" \
      "move contents of current/ into specs/, then 'rmdir .spectacular/current'" "judgment"
    return
  fi

  # Legacy: current/ present without specs/ → mechanical rename available
  if [[ -d "$legacy_dir" && ! -d "$specs_dir" ]]; then
    doc_add "specs" "warning" "$legacy_dir" \
      "legacy current/ folder found — rename to specs/ (current/ deprecated in v0.5.0)" \
      "mv .spectacular/current .spectacular/specs" "mechanical"
    return
  fi

  # specs/ dir present
  if [[ -d "$specs_dir" ]]; then
    doc_add "specs" "pass" "$specs_dir/" "specs/ directory present"
  else
    doc_add "specs" "error" "$specs_dir/" "specs/ directory missing" \
      "mkdir -p .spectacular/specs (mechanical fix available)" "mechanical"
  fi

  # index.md present + parseable
  if [[ -f "$spec_file" ]]; then
    if head -1 "$spec_file" | grep -q '^---$'; then
      doc_add "specs" "pass" "$spec_file" "specs/index.md present with frontmatter"
    else
      doc_add "specs" "error" "$spec_file" "specs/index.md missing frontmatter delimiter" \
        "add proper frontmatter block" "judgment"
    fi
  else
    doc_add "specs" "error" "$spec_file" "specs/index.md missing" \
      "re-scaffold via 'spectacular doctor --fix' or 'spectacular init'" "mechanical"
  fi

  # Check: No nested subdirectories under specs/ (OKF flat specs rule)
  local nested_dirs=()
  shopt -s nullglob
  for subdir in "$specs_dir"/*/; do
    nested_dirs+=("$subdir")
  done
  shopt -u nullglob
  if (( ${#nested_dirs[@]} > 0 )); then
    doc_add "specs" "warning" "$specs_dir/" "nested directory found in specs/ (OKF specs must be flat concept files): ${nested_dirs[*]}" \
      "flatten directories by moving SPEC.md files to flat concept files and removing subdirectories" "judgment"
  fi

  # Flat contract docs: top-level .md files in specs/ (excluding index.md).
  # Two layers per file: (1) structural — frontmatter delimiter present
  # (error-class, mirrors check_frontmatter); (2) schema — required keys, ISO
  # date, closed status enum, conditional version (warning-class).
  #
  # Schema note (spec-audit-mode, b11): capability specs use their OWN required
  # set — status, updated, summary, related — which deliberately differs from the
  # root-anchor set in check_frontmatter (version, updated, summary). Specs make
  # `version:` conditional on `status: published` (a draft has no contract to
  # version) and add `related:`. This fork is intentional and NOT unified with
  # check_frontmatter — findings surface under `specs`, where a user running
  # `doctor specs` expects them. `related:` *resolution* stays with check_links
  # (root-aware target checks); here we only assert the key is present. index.md
  # is a different doc-class (catalog, not capability) and is skipped — it
  # legitimately carries no `status:`.
  local spec_required_fields="status updated summary related"
  # Wayfinding names are canonical; draft/published remain compatibility aliases.
  local spec_status_enum="draft unconfirmed approved implemented superseded deprecated archived"
  shopt -s nullglob
  for contract_doc in "$specs_dir"/*.md; do
    local basename
    basename="$(basename "$contract_doc")"
    [[ "$basename" == "index.md" ]] && continue

    # (1) Structural: frontmatter delimiter (error if broken — matches
    # check_frontmatter's delimiter=error / key=warning split).
    if ! head -1 "$contract_doc" 2>/dev/null | grep -q '^---$'; then
      doc_add "specs" "warning" "$contract_doc" "capability spec missing frontmatter delimiter" \
        "add proper frontmatter block" "judgment"
      continue
    fi
    doc_add "specs" "pass" "$contract_doc" "capability spec present (flat file in specs/)"

    # Extract frontmatter block (between the first two ---).
    local sfm
    sfm=$(awk '/^---$/ { count++; if (count == 2) exit; next } count == 1' "$contract_doc")

    # (2a) Required keys present.
    local field
    for field in $spec_required_fields; do
      if ! echo "$sfm" | grep -q "^${field}:"; then
        doc_add "specs" "warning" "$contract_doc" "capability spec missing required field: ${field}" \
          "add \`${field}:\` to frontmatter" "judgment"
      fi
    done

    # (2b) ISO date on updated: (reuses the check_frontmatter pattern).
    local s_updated
    s_updated=$(echo "$sfm" | awk -F': ' '/^updated:/ { print $2; exit }' | tr -d '"' | tr -d "'")
    if [[ -n "$s_updated" ]] && ! [[ "$s_updated" =~ ^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$ ]]; then
      doc_add "specs" "warning" "$contract_doc" "\`updated:\` not in ISO format (got: $s_updated)" \
        "use YYYY-MM-DD format" "judgment"
    fi

    # (2c) Closed status enum + (2d) conditional version.
    local s_status
    s_status=$(echo "$sfm" | awk -F': ' '/^status:/ { print $2; exit }' | tr -d '"' | tr -d "'" | xargs)
    if [[ -n "$s_status" ]]; then
      case " $spec_status_enum " in
        *" $s_status "*) ;;
        *) doc_add "specs" "warning" "$contract_doc" "\`status: $s_status\` outside allowed set ($spec_status_enum)" \
             "use one of: ${spec_status_enum// /, }" "judgment" ;;
      esac
      if [[ "$s_status" == implemented ]]; then
        for field in implemented_at verified_against; do
          echo "$sfm" | grep -q "^${field}:" || doc_add "specs" "warning" "$contract_doc" "implemented spec missing required evidence field: $field" \
            "record the historical implementation evidence" "judgment"
        done
      fi
    fi
  done
  shopt -u nullglob

  # Delta integrity (v1.28.0+): validate each active request's SPEC-DELTA.md
  # against the current spec files. MODIFIED/REMOVED must quote a bullet that
  # exists; ADDED must not duplicate one. NONE is always valid. This replaces the
  # date heuristic below as the primary drift signal (heuristic stays as backstop).
  for delta in "$SPEC_REQUESTS_DIR"/*/SPEC-DELTA.md; do
    [[ -f "$delta" ]] || continue
    local dslug; dslug="$(basename "$(dirname "$delta")")"
    # NONE line → valid, nothing to check.
    if grep -qE '^NONE( |$|—|-)' "$delta"; then
      doc_add "specs" "pass" "$delta" "spec delta declares NONE (no capability change)"
      continue
    fi
    # Must have at least one section heading if not NONE.
    if ! grep -qE '^### (ADDED|MODIFIED|REMOVED)' "$delta"; then
      doc_add "specs" "warning" "$delta" "SPEC-DELTA.md has no ADDED/MODIFIED/REMOVED section and isn't NONE" \
        "declare spec impact as delta sections, or 'NONE — <why>'" "judgment"
      continue
    fi
    local section="" line file payload cur ok=1
    while IFS= read -r line; do
      case "$line" in
        '### ADDED')    section="ADDED";    continue ;;
        '### MODIFIED') section="MODIFIED"; continue ;;
        '### REMOVED')  section="REMOVED";  continue ;;
        '### '*)        section="";         continue ;;
      esac
      [[ "$line" =~ ^-\ .*::.* ]] || continue   # only `- <file> :: <payload>` lines
      file="${line#- }"; file="${file%% ::*}"; file="$(echo "$file" | sed 's/[[:space:]]*$//')"
      payload="${line#*:: }"
      local target="$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/$file"
      [[ -f "$target" ]] || { doc_add "specs" "warning" "$delta" "delta targets missing file: $file (for $dslug)" "fix the file path in SPEC-DELTA.md" "judgment"; ok=0; continue; }
      case "$section" in
        MODIFIED|REMOVED)
          # payload's current side is the first quoted string.
          cur="$(echo "$payload" | sed -E 's/^"([^"]*)".*/\1/')"
          if [[ -n "$cur" ]] && ! grep -qF -- "$cur" "$target"; then
            doc_add "specs" "warning" "$delta" "$section delta quotes a bullet not found in $file: \"$cur\" ($dslug)" \
              "quote the current bullet verbatim, or fix the delta" "judgment"; ok=0
          fi ;;
        ADDED)
          if grep -qF -- "$payload" "$target"; then
            doc_add "specs" "warning" "$delta" "ADDED delta duplicates an existing bullet in $file ($dslug)" \
              "remove the duplicate — it's already present" "judgment"; ok=0
          fi ;;
      esac
    done < "$delta"
    (( ok == 1 )) && doc_add "specs" "pass" "$delta" "spec delta integrity ok ($dslug)"
  done

  # Drift: specs/index.md staler than the newest archived request
  if [[ -f "$spec_file" ]] && head -1 "$spec_file" | grep -q '^---$'; then
    local spec_updated newest_arch="" newest_epoch=0 spec_epoch
    spec_updated=$(fm_get "$spec_file" "updated")
    spec_epoch=$(_date_to_epoch "$spec_updated")
    for arch_plan in "$SPEC_ARCHIVE_DIR"/*/PLAN.md; do
      [[ -f "$arch_plan" ]] || continue
      local a_upd a_epoch
      a_upd=$(fm_get "$arch_plan" "updated")
      a_epoch=$(_date_to_epoch "$a_upd")
      if (( a_epoch > newest_epoch )); then
        newest_epoch=$a_epoch
        newest_arch="$(basename "$(dirname "$arch_plan")")"
      fi
    done
    if (( newest_epoch > 0 && spec_epoch > 0 && newest_epoch > spec_epoch )); then
      doc_add "specs" "warning" "$spec_file" \
        "specs/index.md (updated $spec_updated) may be stale — request '$newest_arch' archived more recently; run spec-sync to confirm it's reflected" \
        "review specs/index.md against archive/$newest_arch and update if a capability is missing" "judgment"
    fi
  fi

  shopt -u nullglob
}

# ── area: docs (slim discovery — v1.2.0+) ────────────────────────────────────
# Schema validation, frontmatter checks, orphan detection, and renderer config
# all moved to pageworks. Spectacular now reports only what it observes about
# docs/: folder presence, manifest presence, and whether pageworks is installed.
# Anyone needing the full validation surface should run `pageworks doctor`.
check_docs() {
  local docs_dir="docs"
  local manifest="${docs_dir}/docs.yaml"

  # No docs/ at all → skip silently (docs are opt-in)
  if [[ ! -d "$docs_dir" ]]; then
    return 0
  fi

  doc_add "docs" "pass" "$docs_dir" "docs/ folder present"

  # Manifest discovery — pageworks handles its absence as an init prompt.
  if [[ -f "$manifest" ]]; then
    doc_add "docs" "pass" "$manifest" "docs.yaml manifest present"
  else
    doc_add "docs" "info" "$manifest" "docs.yaml not found — run 'pageworks init' to scaffold one" \
      "pageworks owns docs/ schema and authoring" "judgment"
  fi

  # Pageworks install discovery — non-blocking; install hint only.
  if command -v pageworks >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    doc_add "docs" "pass" "pageworks" "pageworks CLI available — run 'pageworks doctor' for full validation"
  else
    doc_add "docs" "info" "pageworks" "pageworks not installed — public-doc validation moved to pageworks in v1.2.0" \
      "install: https://github.com/alexsmedile/pageworks" "judgment"
  fi
}

# ── area: personas (v1.3.0+ — opt-in) ────────────────────────────────────────
# PERSONAS.md is an opt-in canonical doc. Absent → skip with info. Present →
# validate frontmatter + at least one persona block + at least one story per
# persona. Never errors on absence.
check_personas() {
  [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]] || return 0

  local pf="$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/PERSONAS.md"

  if [[ ! -f "$pf" ]]; then
    doc_add "personas" "info" "$pf" "PERSONAS.md not scaffolded — opt-in via 'spectacular init --with personas' or product/content kits" \
      "skip" "judgment"
    return 0
  fi

  # Frontmatter present
  if head -1 "$pf" | grep -q '^---$'; then
    doc_add "personas" "pass" "$pf" "PERSONAS.md present with frontmatter"
  else
    doc_add "personas" "error" "$pf" "PERSONAS.md missing frontmatter delimiter" \
      "add proper frontmatter block" "judgment"
    return 0
  fi

  # Count persona blocks (lines starting with "## " in body, skipping placeholder).
  # Only the first two `---` lines are frontmatter delimiters; later `---` are
  # visual separators between persona blocks and must not toggle the fm state.
  local persona_count
  persona_count=$(awk '
    /^---$/ && fm_seen < 2 { fm = !fm; fm_seen++; next }
    !fm && /^## / && !/^## <Persona/ { count++ }
    END { print count + 0 }
  ' "$pf")

  if [[ "$persona_count" -eq 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "personas" "warning" "$pf" "PERSONAS.md has no filled persona blocks (only placeholders)" \
      "replace '## <Persona name>' placeholders with real persona blocks" "judgment"
    return 0
  fi

  doc_add "personas" "pass" "$pf" "${persona_count} persona block(s) found"

  # Soft warn: >5 personas
  if [[ "$persona_count" -gt 5 ]]; then
    doc_add "personas" "warning" "$pf" "${persona_count} personas — >5 typically signals decoration; consider merging or cutting" \
      "ask: would removing one change a build decision? if no, cut it" "judgment"
  fi

  # Per-persona story count: each persona block (## heading) must contain ≥1
  # story line ("- As ..."). Awk walks blocks and reports any block with zero.
  local empty_personas
  empty_personas=$(awk '
    /^---$/ && fm_seen < 2 { fm = !fm; fm_seen++; next }
    !fm && /^## / && !/^## <Persona/ {
      if (in_block && story_count_in_block == 0) {
        empty_names = empty_names ? empty_names ", " current : current
      }
      current = $0
      sub(/^## /, "", current)
      in_block = 1
      story_count_in_block = 0
      next
    }
    !fm && in_block && /^- As / { story_count_in_block++ }
    END {
      if (in_block && story_count_in_block == 0) {
        empty_names = empty_names ? empty_names ", " current : current
      }
      print empty_names
    }
  ' "$pf")

  local total_story_count
  total_story_count=$(grep -c '^- As ' "$pf" || true)

  if [[ -n "$empty_personas" ]]; then
    doc_add "personas" "warning" "$pf" "persona(s) without stories: ${empty_personas}" \
      "each persona needs ≥1 'As X, I want Y, so Z' story; persona without stories is decoration" "judgment"
  fi

  if [[ "$total_story_count" -gt 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "personas" "pass" "$pf" "${total_story_count} user story line(s) across ${persona_count} persona(s)"
  else
    doc_add "personas" "warning" "$pf" "no user stories found (expected 'As X, I want Y, so Z' format)" \
      "add stories to each persona" "judgment"
  fi
}

# ── check_memory (v1.5.0+) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Soft-DB self-check: index ↔ entries drift, frontmatter shape.
check_memory() {
  [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]] || return 0
  local idx="$SPEC_MEMORIES_DIR/index.md" dir="$SPEC_MEMORIES_DIR"

  if [[ ! -f "$idx" ]] && [[ ! -d "$dir" ]]; then
    doc_add "memory" "info" "$idx" "memories/index.md not scaffolded — opt-in via 'spectacular init --with memory' or coding kit" \
      "skip" "judgment"
    return 0
  fi

  if [[ ! -f "$idx" ]]; then
    doc_add "memory" "warning" "$idx" "memories/ directory exists but memories/index.md index is missing" \
      "run 'spectacular remember \"...\"' to regenerate the index, or scaffold memories/index.md manually" "judgment"
    return 0
  fi

  if head -1 "$idx" | grep -q '^---$'; then
    doc_add "memory" "pass" "$idx" "memories/index.md present with frontmatter"
  else
    doc_add "memory" "warning" "$idx" "memories/index.md missing frontmatter delimiter" \
      "add proper frontmatter block (type: index, doc: memory, updated: <date>)" "judgment"
  fi

  # Count entries
  local entry_count=0 file
  if [[ -d "$dir" ]]; then
    for file in "$dir"/*.md; do
      [[ -f "$file" ]] || continue
      # Don't count index.md as a memory entry file
      [[ "$(basename "$file")" == "index.md" ]] && continue
      entry_count=$((entry_count + 1))
    done
  fi

  if [[ $entry_count -eq 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "memory" "info" "$dir" "no memory entries yet"
    return 0
  fi

  for file in "$dir"/*.md; do
    [[ -f "$file" && "$(basename "$file")" != index.md ]] || continue
    local memory_status; memory_status=$(fm_get "$file" status)
    case "$memory_status" in active|superseded|retracted) ;; "") doc_add "memory" "warning" "$file" "memory has no lifecycle status (legacy-readable)" "add status: active or migrate explicitly" "judgment" ;; *) doc_add "memory" "warning" "$file" "invalid memory status: $memory_status" "use active|superseded|retracted" "judgment" ;; esac
    [[ "$memory_status" != retracted || -n "$(fm_get "$file" retraction_reason)" ]] || doc_add "memory" "warning" "$file" "retracted memory lacks retraction_reason" "record why the fact was withdrawn" "judgment"
  done

  # Detect index ↔ entries drift
  local index_links
  index_links=$(grep -oE '\[\[memories/[^]]+\]\]' "$idx" 2>/dev/null | sed 's/\[\[memories\///; s/\]\]//' | sort -u || true)
  local index_link_count
  index_link_count=$(echo "$index_links" | grep -c . || true)

  if [[ $entry_count -ne $index_link_count ]]; then
    doc_add "memory" "warning" "$idx" "drift: ${entry_count} entries on disk vs ${index_link_count} links in memories/index.md" \
      "regenerate by writing or removing an entry — any 'spectacular remember' call rebuilds the index" "judgment"
  else
    doc_add "memory" "pass" "$dir" "${entry_count} memory entries; index ↔ entries in sync"
  fi

  # Staleness check (v1.16.0+): flag memory entries older than 180 days.
  local _stale_count=0 _stale_slugs="" _now_epoch _entry_epoch _age_days _updated
  _now_epoch=$(date "+%s")
  if [[ -d "$dir" ]]; then
    for file in "$dir"/*.md; do
      [[ -f "$file" ]] || continue
      [[ "$(basename "$file")" == "index.md" ]] && continue
      _updated=$(fm_get "$file" "updated" 2>/dev/null || true)
      [[ -z "$_updated" ]] && continue
      # Parse ISO date YYYY-MM-DD; skip if not that shape
      [[ "$_updated" =~ ^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$ ]] || continue
      _entry_epoch=$(date -j -f "%Y-%m-%d" "$_updated" "+%s" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)
      [[ "$_entry_epoch" -eq 0 ]] && continue
      _age_days=$(( (_now_epoch - _entry_epoch) / 86400 ))
      if [[ $_age_days -gt 180 ]]; then
        _stale_count=$((_stale_count + 1))
        local _mslug; _mslug=$(basename "$file" .md)
        _stale_slugs="${_stale_slugs:+$_stale_slugs, }$_mslug (${_age_days}d)"
      fi
    done
  fi
  if [[ $_stale_count -gt 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "memory" "warning" "$dir" \
      "${_stale_count} memory $([ $_stale_count -eq 1 ] && echo entry || echo entries) older than 180 days: ${_stale_slugs}" \
      "review and update or archive stale entries" "judgment"
  fi

  # Check 5: Prefix naming pattern M<N>-<slug>.md
  local invalid_prefix_count=0 invalid_prefix_files=""
  for file in "$dir"/*.md; do
    [[ -f "$file" ]] || continue
    local bname; bname=$(basename "$file")
    [[ "$bname" == "index.md" ]] && continue
    if [[ ! "$bname" =~ ^M[0-9]+-[a-z0-9-]+.md$ ]]; then
      invalid_prefix_count=$((invalid_prefix_count + 1))
      invalid_prefix_files="${invalid_prefix_files:+$invalid_prefix_files, }$bname"
    fi
  done
  if [[ $invalid_prefix_count -gt 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "memory" "warning" "$dir" \
      "$invalid_prefix_count memory file(s) missing sequential M<N>-<slug> prefix: $invalid_prefix_files" \
      "rename files to follow the M<N>-<slug>.md pattern" "judgment"
  fi

}

# ── check_sessions (v1.5.0+) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Soft-DB + lifecycle: at most one open, 4h stale-open warning.
check_sessions() {
  [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]] || return 0
  local idx="$SPEC_SESSIONS_DIR/index.md" dir="$SPEC_SESSIONS_DIR"

  if [[ ! -f "$idx" ]] && [[ ! -d "$dir" ]]; then
    doc_add "sessions" "info" "$idx" "sessions/index.md not scaffolded — opt-in via 'spectacular init --with sessions' or coding kit" \
      "skip" "judgment"
    return 0
  fi

  if [[ ! -f "$idx" ]]; then
    doc_add "sessions" "warning" "$idx" "sessions/ directory exists but sessions/index.md index is missing" \
      "run 'spectacular session start' to regenerate the index" "judgment"
    return 0
  fi

  if head -1 "$idx" | grep -q '^---$'; then
    doc_add "sessions" "pass" "$idx" "sessions/index.md present with frontmatter"
  else
    doc_add "sessions" "warning" "$idx" "sessions/index.md missing frontmatter delimiter" \
      "add proper frontmatter block (type: index, doc: sessions, updated: <date>)" "judgment"
  fi

  # Count entries + open sessions
  local entry_count=0 open_count=0 open_slugs="" stale_slugs="" file status start
  if [[ -d "$dir" ]]; then
    for file in "$dir"/*.md; do
      [[ -f "$file" ]] || continue
      [[ "$(basename "$file")" == "index.md" ]] && continue
      entry_count=$((entry_count + 1))
      status=$(fm_get "$file" "status")
      if [[ "$status" == "open" ]]; then
        open_count=$((open_count + 1))
        local slug
        slug=$(basename "$file" .md)
        open_slugs="${open_slugs:+$open_slugs, }$slug"
        # 4h staleness check (per D7)
        start=$(fm_get "$file" "start_date")
        if [[ -n "$start" ]]; then
          local start_epoch now_epoch age_seconds
          start_epoch=$(date -j -f "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S" "$start" "+%s" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)
          now_epoch=$(date "+%s")
          age_seconds=$((now_epoch - start_epoch))
          if [[ $start_epoch -gt 0 ]] && [[ $age_seconds -gt 14400 ]]; then
            stale_slugs="${stale_slugs:+$stale_slugs, }$slug"
          fi
        fi
      fi
    done
  fi

  if [[ $entry_count -eq 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "sessions" "info" "$dir" "no session entries yet"
    return 0
  fi

  # Lifecycle invariant: ≤1 open
  if [[ $open_count -gt 1 ]]; then
    doc_add "sessions" "error" "$dir" "lifecycle violation: ${open_count} sessions open simultaneously ($open_slugs)" \
      "close all but one with 'spectacular session end' (manually edit the others if needed)" "judgment"
  elif [[ $open_count -eq 1 ]]; then
    doc_add "sessions" "info" "$dir" "1 session open: $open_slugs"
  fi

  # Stale-open warning (>4h)
  if [[ -n "$stale_slugs" ]]; then
    doc_add "sessions" "warning" "$dir" "open session(s) >4h old: $stale_slugs" \
      "close with 'spectacular session end' if work is done; otherwise --ignore-stale (TBD)" "judgment"
  fi

  # Drift check (entries vs index rows)
  local index_links
  index_links=$(grep -oE '\[\[sessions/[^]]+\]\]' "$idx" 2>/dev/null | sed 's/\[\[sessions\///; s/\]\]//' | sort -u || true)
  local index_link_count
  index_link_count=$(echo "$index_links" | grep -c . || true)

  if [[ $entry_count -ne $index_link_count ]]; then
    doc_add "sessions" "warning" "$idx" "drift: ${entry_count} entries on disk vs ${index_link_count} links in sessions/index.md" \
      "regenerate by running any 'spectacular session start' or 'session end' — both rebuild the index" "judgment"
  else
    doc_add "sessions" "pass" "$dir" "${entry_count} session entries; index ↔ entries in sync"
  fi
}

# ── check_feedback (v1.6.0+) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Judgment-only area (no --fix). Flags:
#   - open entries older than 30 days
#   - missing required frontmatter fields
#   - orphan back-refs (PLAN feedback: list mentions a missing file, or
#     entry's request: field points to a missing request)
check_feedback() {
  [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]] || return 0

  local top_dir="$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/feedbacks"
  local has_any=false

  if [[ -d "$top_dir" ]] || ls -d "$SPEC_REQUESTS_DIR"/*/feedbacks >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    has_any=true
  fi

  if ! $has_any; then
    doc_add "feedback" "info" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/feedbacks/" "no feedback entries yet — start one with 'spectacular feedback-loop new <target>'" \
      "skip" "judgment"
    return 0
  fi

  local entry_count=0 open_count=0 stale_count=0 malformed_count=0 orphan_count=0
  local stale_slugs="" malformed_files="" orphan_files=""
  local now_epoch threshold_epoch
  now_epoch=$(date "+%s")
  # 30 days = 2592000 seconds
  threshold_epoch=$((now_epoch - 2592000))

  local f
  while IFS= read -r f; do
    [[ -z "$f" ]] && continue
    entry_count=$((entry_count + 1))

    # Required fields
    local type_v status_v opened_v target_v request_v
    type_v=$(fm_get "$f" "type")
    status_v=$(fm_get "$f" "status")
    opened_v=$(fm_get "$f" "opened")
    target_v=$(fm_get "$f" "target")
    request_v=$(fm_get "$f" "request")

    if [[ "$type_v" != "feedback" ]] || [[ -z "$status_v" ]] || [[ -z "$opened_v" ]] || [[ -z "$target_v" ]]; then
      malformed_count=$((malformed_count + 1))
      malformed_files="${malformed_files:+$malformed_files, }$(basename "$f")"
      continue
    fi

    if [[ "$status_v" == "open" ]]; then
      open_count=$((open_count + 1))
      local opened_epoch
      opened_epoch=$(date -j -f "%Y-%m-%d" "$opened_v" "+%s" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)
      if [[ $opened_epoch -gt 0 && $opened_epoch -lt $threshold_epoch ]]; then
        stale_count=$((stale_count + 1))
        stale_slugs="${stale_slugs:+$stale_slugs, }$(basename "$f" .md)"
      fi
    fi

    # Orphan back-ref: request: field set but request folder missing
    if [[ -n "$request_v" && "$request_v" != "null" ]]; then
      if [[ ! -d "$SPEC_REQUESTS_DIR/$request_v" ]]; then
        orphan_count=$((orphan_count + 1))
        orphan_files="${orphan_files:+$orphan_files, }$(basename "$f" .md)→$request_v"
      fi
    fi
  done < <(_feedback_iter_all)

  if [[ $entry_count -eq 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "feedback" "info" "$top_dir" "no feedback entries yet"
    return 0
  fi

  doc_add "feedback" "pass" "$top_dir" "$entry_count feedback entries ($open_count open)"

  if [[ $malformed_count -gt 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "feedback" "warning" "$top_dir" "$malformed_count entries missing required frontmatter ($malformed_files)" \
      "ensure type, status, opened, and target fields are set; see references/feedback-rules.md" "judgment"
  fi

  if [[ $stale_count -gt 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "feedback" "warning" "$top_dir" "$stale_count open entries stale (>30 days): $stale_slugs" \
      "resolve with 'spectacular feedback-loop resolve <slug>' or mark parked" "judgment"
  fi

  if [[ $orphan_count -gt 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "feedback" "warning" "$top_dir" "$orphan_count entries reference a missing request: $orphan_files" \
      "unset request: field or restore the request folder" "judgment"
  fi
}

# ── check_ideas (v1.7.0+) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Judgment-only — no --fix. Flags stale exploring, orphan promoted, malformed.
check_ideas() {
  [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]] || return 0

  local top_dir="$SPEC_IDEAS_DIR"

  if [[ ! -d "$top_dir" ]]; then
    doc_add "ideas" "info" "$top_dir" "no ideas/ folder — opt-in via 'spectacular idea new <slug>'" \
      "skip" "judgment"
    return 0
  fi

  local entry_count=0 exploring_count=0 stale_count=0 malformed_count=0 orphan_count=0 unknown_status_count=0
  local stale_slugs="" malformed_files="" orphan_files="" unknown_files=""
  local now_epoch threshold_epoch
  now_epoch=$(date "+%s")
  # 90 days = 7776000 seconds
  threshold_epoch=$((now_epoch - 7776000))

  local f
  while IFS= read -r f; do
    [[ -z "$f" ]] && continue
    entry_count=$((entry_count + 1))

    local type_v status_v updated_v
    type_v=$(fm_get "$f" "type")
    status_v=$(fm_get "$f" "status")
    updated_v=$(fm_get "$f" "updated")

    if [[ "$type_v" != "idea" ]] || [[ -z "$status_v" ]] || [[ -z "$updated_v" ]]; then
      malformed_count=$((malformed_count + 1))
      malformed_files="${malformed_files:+$malformed_files, }$(basename "$f")"
      continue
    fi

    case "$status_v" in
      parked) ;;
      exploring)
        exploring_count=$((exploring_count + 1))
        local updated_epoch
        updated_epoch=$(date -j -f "%Y-%m-%d" "$updated_v" "+%s" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)
        if [[ $updated_epoch -gt 0 && $updated_epoch -lt $threshold_epoch ]]; then
          stale_count=$((stale_count + 1))
          stale_slugs="${stale_slugs:+$stale_slugs, }$(basename "$f" .md)"
        fi
        ;;
      promoted)
        # Orphan: status: promoted but file is still in live ideas/ (should be in archive/ideas/)
        orphan_count=$((orphan_count + 1))
        orphan_files="${orphan_files:+$orphan_files, }$(basename "$f" .md)"
        ;;
      *)
        unknown_status_count=$((unknown_status_count + 1))
        unknown_files="${unknown_files:+$unknown_files, }$(basename "$f" .md)→$status_v"
        ;;
    esac
  done < <(_iter_md ideas)

  if [[ $entry_count -eq 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "ideas" "info" "$top_dir" "no ideas yet — start one with 'spectacular idea new <slug>'"
    return 0
  fi

  doc_add "ideas" "pass" "$top_dir" "$entry_count idea(s) ($exploring_count exploring)"

  if [[ $malformed_count -gt 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "ideas" "warning" "$top_dir" "$malformed_count entries missing required frontmatter ($malformed_files)" \
      "ensure type, status, updated fields are set; see references/idea-rules.md" "judgment"
  fi

  if [[ $stale_count -gt 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "ideas" "warning" "$top_dir" "$stale_count exploring idea(s) stale (>90 days): $stale_slugs" \
      "decide: promote, demote to parked, or delete" "judgment"
  fi

  if [[ $orphan_count -gt 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "ideas" "warning" "$top_dir" "$orphan_count promoted idea(s) still in ideas/ — should be in archive/ideas/ ($orphan_files)" \
      "move file to .spectacular/archive/ideas/ or rerun 'spectacular idea promote'" "judgment"
  fi

  if [[ $unknown_status_count -gt 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "ideas" "warning" "$top_dir" "$unknown_status_count entries with unknown status ($unknown_files)" \
      "use one of: parked | exploring | promoted" "judgment"
  fi
}

# ── check_wayfinding ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Validates canonical IDs and the blocked_by DAG. Derived fog/frontier remains
# read-only; doctor catches the structural defects that would make it lie.
check_wayfinding() {
  [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]] || return 0
  local tmp nodes edges f id dep dep_file count=0 malformed="" duplicate="" dangling=""
  tmp=$(mktemp -d)
  nodes="$tmp/nodes"; edges="$tmp/edges"
  : > "$nodes"; : > "$edges"

  local collection base slug_key slug_seen="$tmp/slugs" slug_duplicates=""
  : > "$slug_seen"
  for collection in ideas questions research spikes decisions specs; do
    for f in "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/$collection"/*.md; do
      [[ -f "$f" && "$(basename "$f")" != index.md ]] || continue
      base=$(basename "$f" .md)
      slug_key=$(printf '%s' "$base" | sed -E 's/^(DEC|QUE|IDEA|RES|SPK|SPC)-[0-9]+-//; s/^D[0-9]+-//')
      if grep -q "^${collection}|${slug_key}$" "$slug_seen"; then
        slug_duplicates="${slug_duplicates:+$slug_duplicates, }$collection/$slug_key"
      else
        printf '%s|%s\n' "$collection" "$slug_key" >> "$slug_seen"
      fi
    done
  done
  [[ -z "$slug_duplicates" ]] || doc_add "wayfinding" "error" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/" "duplicate slug(s) within a collection: $slug_duplicates" \
    "rename one record through an explicit, reference-aware migration" "judgment"

  while IFS= read -r f; do
    id=$(fm_get "$f" id)
    [[ -n "$id" ]] || continue
    count=$((count + 1))
    if ! _is_uuidv7 "$id" && [[ ! "$id" =~ ^(QUE|RES|SPK|SPC)-[0-9]{3,}$ ]]; then
      malformed="${malformed:+$malformed, }$id"
    fi
    if grep -q "^${id}|" "$nodes" 2>/dev/null; then
      duplicate="${duplicate:+$duplicate, }$id"
    else
      printf '%s|%s\n' "$id" "$f" >> "$nodes"
    fi
    while IFS= read -r dep; do
      [[ -n "$dep" ]] || continue
      printf '%s|%s\n' "$id" "$dep" >> "$edges"
    done < <(_fm_list "$f" blocked_by)
  done < <(_wayfind_iter)

  while IFS= read -r f; do
    case "$(fm_get "$f" type):$(fm_get "$f" status)" in research:completed|spike:completed)
      case "$(fm_get "$f" result)" in supported|refuted|inconclusive) ;; *) doc_add "wayfinding" "warning" "$f" "completed discovery has invalid/missing result" "use supported|refuted|inconclusive" "judgment" ;; esac
      grep -q '^\*\*Evidence:\*\* .\+' "$f" || doc_add "wayfinding" "warning" "$f" "completed discovery has no concrete evidence" "record sources/artifacts before completion" "judgment"
      ;;
    esac
  done < <(_wayfind_iter)

  if (( count == 0 )); then
    rm -rf "$tmp"
    doc_add "wayfinding" "info" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/" "no canonical discovery nodes yet"
    return 0
  fi

  while IFS='|' read -r id dep; do
    [[ -n "$id" && -n "$dep" ]] || continue
    if ! _is_uuidv7 "$dep" && [[ ! "$dep" =~ ^(DEC|QUE|IDEA|RES|SPK|PRT|SPC|TSK)-[0-9]{3,}$ ]]; then
      malformed="${malformed:+$malformed, }${id}→${dep}"
      continue
    fi
    dep_file=$(_wayfind_find_id "$dep") || dangling="${dangling:+$dangling, }${id}→${dep}"
  done < "$edges"

  [[ -z "$malformed" ]] || doc_add "wayfinding" "warning" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/" "non-canonical ID/reference(s): $malformed" \
    "normalize with 'spectacular id resolve'; persist canonical IDs" "judgment"
  [[ -z "$duplicate" ]] || doc_add "wayfinding" "error" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/" "duplicate canonical ID(s): $duplicate" \
    "assign a unique ID and rewrite inbound references" "judgment"
  [[ -z "$dangling" ]] || doc_add "wayfinding" "warning" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/" "dangling dependency reference(s): $dangling" \
    "create/restore the referenced node or remove the stale edge" "judgment"

  local cycle
  cycle=$(awk -F'|' '
    NR==FNR { node[$1]=1; next }
    { adj[$1]=adj[$1] " " $2 }
    function visit(n,   parts,i,m,nxt) {
      if (color[n] == 1) { cycle=n; return 1 }
      if (color[n] == 2) return 0
      color[n]=1
      m=split(adj[n], parts, " ")
      for (i=1; i<=m; i++) {
        nxt=parts[i]
        if (nxt != "" && node[nxt] && visit(nxt)) { cycle=n " → " cycle; return 1 }
      }
      color[n]=2
      return 0
    }
    END {
      for (n in node) if (color[n] == 0 && visit(n)) { print cycle; exit }
    }
  ' "$nodes" "$edges")
  [[ -z "$cycle" ]] || doc_add "wayfinding" "error" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/" "dependency cycle: $cycle" \
    "remove or reverse one blocked_by edge; a DAG cannot contain cycles" "judgment"

  # Dependencies outrank target versions. Compare the full SemVer base and the
  # discovery/execution phase so an earlier target cannot depend on later work.
  local inversions="" node_target dep_target node_weight dep_weight
  while IFS='|' read -r id dep; do
    [[ -n "$id" && -n "$dep" ]] || continue
    f=$(awk -F'|' -v id="$id" '$1==id {print $2; exit}' "$nodes")
    dep_file=$(_wayfind_find_id "$dep") || continue
    node_target=$(fm_get "$f" target_version); dep_target=$(fm_get "$dep_file" target_version)
    node_weight=$(_wayfind_target_weight "$node_target" 2>/dev/null) || continue
    dep_weight=$(_wayfind_target_weight "$dep_target" 2>/dev/null) || continue
    if (( node_weight < dep_weight )); then
      inversions="${inversions:+$inversions, }$id($node_target)→$dep($dep_target)"
    fi
  done < "$edges"
  [[ -z "$inversions" ]] || doc_add "wayfinding" "warning" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/" "target-version inversion(s): $inversions" \
    "move the dependent target later or the prerequisite earlier; dependencies win, never reslot silently" "judgment"

  # Infer only strong prose signals. This is advisory: explicit frontmatter is
  # still the graph authority, and doctor never writes an inferred edge.
  local undeclared="" signal_files="" line ref declared source_id source_set plan_ref plan_set
  local scan_files=()
  [[ -f "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/PRD.md" ]] && scan_files+=("$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/PRD.md")
  [[ -f "$SPEC_ROADMAPS_DIR/index.md" ]] && scan_files+=("$SPEC_ROADMAPS_DIR/index.md")
  for f in "$SPEC_SPECS_DIR"/*.md "$SPEC_REQUESTS_DIR"/*/PLAN.md; do [[ -f "$f" ]] && scan_files+=("$f"); done
  for f in ${scan_files[@]+"${scan_files[@]}"}; do
    source_id=$(fm_get "$f" id); source_set=" "
    while IFS= read -r declared; do [[ -n "$declared" ]] && source_set+="$declared "; done < <(_fm_list "$f" blocked_by)
    while IFS= read -r line; do
      while IFS= read -r ref; do
        [[ -n "$ref" && "$ref" != "$source_id" ]] || continue
        if [[ -n "$source_id" && "$source_set" != *" $ref "* ]]; then
          undeclared="${undeclared:+$undeclared, }${source_id}→${ref}"
        elif [[ -z "$source_id" ]]; then
          signal_files="${signal_files:+$signal_files, }${f#"$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR"/}→${ref}"
        fi
      done < <(printf '%s\n' "$line" | grep -Eo '([0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-7[0-9a-f]{3}-[89ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}|(DEC|QUE|IDEA|RES|SPK|PRT|SPC|TSK)-[0-9]{3,})' | sort -u)
    done < <(grep -Ei 'depends[- ]on|blocked[- _]by|requires|prerequisite' "$f" 2>/dev/null || true)

    # Request PLAN body links under Dependencies must agree with either side of
    # its frontmatter graph. This catches prose-only request dependencies.
    if [[ "$f" == "$SPEC_REQUESTS_DIR"/*/PLAN.md ]]; then
      plan_set=" "
      while IFS= read -r declared; do [[ -n "$declared" ]] && plan_set+="$declared "; done < <(_fm_list "$f" depends-on)
      while IFS= read -r declared; do [[ -n "$declared" ]] && plan_set+="$declared "; done < <(_fm_list "$f" blocks)
      while IFS= read -r plan_ref; do
        [[ -n "$plan_ref" ]] || continue
        [[ "$plan_set" == *" $plan_ref "* ]] || undeclared="${undeclared:+$undeclared, }$(basename "$(dirname "$f")")→$plan_ref"
      done < <(awk '/^## Dependencies/{on=1;next} /^## /{on=0} on{print}' "$f" \
        | grep -Ei 'depends|blocked|hard dependency|enables' \
        | grep -Eiv 'no dependency|<!--' \
        | grep -Eo '\[\[[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]+\]\]' | tr -d '[]' | sort -u)
    fi
  done
  [[ -z "$undeclared" ]] || doc_add "wayfinding" "warning" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/" "inferred dependency missing from frontmatter: $undeclared" \
    "review the signal, then add blocked_by/depends-on/blocks explicitly or rewrite misleading prose" "judgment"
  [[ -z "$signal_files" ]] || doc_add "wayfinding" "info" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/" "cross-layer dependency signal(s) to review: $signal_files" \
    "confirm the referenced canonical edge is represented by the owning node" "judgment"

  if [[ -z "$malformed$duplicate$dangling$cycle$inversions$undeclared" ]]; then
    doc_add "wayfinding" "pass" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/" "$count canonical discovery node(s); IDs, dependency DAG, and target order are valid"
  fi
  rm -rf "$tmp"
}

# ── check_debug (v1.26.0+) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Validates debug/<slug> trace spines against the schema enums + the cross-field
# invariants an LLM orchestrator drifts on (it hand-writes these JSON files — the
# CLI doesn't scaffold them). Judgment-only, no --fix: catches a bad status/
# disposition value or a wont-fix/folded job that wrongly logged an F<N>, before
# it surfaces later as a resume failure. Enums mirror references/debug-trace.md.
check_debug() {
  [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]] || return 0
  local top_dir="$SPEC_DEBUGS_DIR"

  if [[ ! -d "$top_dir" ]]; then
    doc_add "debug" "info" "$top_dir" "no debugs/ folder — opens on the first fleet job (see references/debug-trace.md)" \
      "skip" "judgment"
    return 0
  fi

  # Source-of-truth enums (references/debug-trace.md). Kept as space-lists for a
  # simple word-membership test — no jq dependency, python only to read JSON.
  local job_status="investigating researching planning fixing verifying resolved folded wont-fix"
  local dispositions="resolved folded-into-request wont-fix"

  local job_count=0 bad="" job d slug
  for d in "$top_dir"/*/; do
    d="${d%/}"   # strip trailing slash so path joins don't double up
    [[ -d "$d" ]] || continue
    slug=$(basename "$d")
    job="$d/job.json"
    [[ -f "$job" ]] || { bad=1; doc_add "debug" "warning" "$d" "debugs/$slug has no job.json spine" \
        "every debug job needs a job.json — see references/debug-trace.md, or remove a stray folder" "judgment"; continue; }
    job_count=$((job_count + 1))

    # Read the fields we validate in one python call (empty string if absent/unparseable).
    local fields status sclass
    fields=$(python3 -c '
import json,sys
try:
    d=json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))
except Exception as e:
    print("__PARSE_ERROR__"); sys.exit(0)
print(d.get("status","")); print(d.get("symptom_class",""))
' "$job" 2>/dev/null)

    if [[ "$fields" == "__PARSE_ERROR__"* ]]; then
      bad=1; doc_add "debug" "warning" "$job" "debugs/$slug/job.json does not parse as JSON" \
        "fix the JSON syntax; validate with: python3 -m json.tool $job" "judgment"
      continue
    fi
    status=$(printf '%s\n' "$fields" | sed -n '1p')
    sclass=$(printf '%s\n' "$fields" | sed -n '2p')

    # status enum (this is the field the orchestrator put a reason-value into)
    if [[ -n "$status" ]] && [[ " $job_status " != *" $status "* ]]; then
      bad=1; doc_add "debug" "warning" "$job" "debugs/$slug: job status '$status' is off-enum" \
        "use one of: ${job_status// / | } (a 'reason' value like needs-more-context belongs in a hypotheses-only investigation, not job status)" "judgment"
    fi

    # outcome.json: disposition enum + the no-fix-on-decline invariant
    local outcome="$d/outcome.json"
    if [[ -f "$outcome" ]]; then
      local ofields disp nfixes
      ofields=$(python3 -c '
import json,sys
try:
    d=json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))
except Exception:
    print("__PARSE_ERROR__"); sys.exit(0)
print(d.get("disposition",""))
lf=d.get("logged_fixes",[])
print(len(lf) if isinstance(lf,list) else -1)
' "$outcome" 2>/dev/null)
      if [[ "$ofields" == "__PARSE_ERROR__"* ]]; then
        bad=1; doc_add "debug" "warning" "$outcome" "debugs/$slug/outcome.json does not parse as JSON" \
          "fix the JSON syntax; validate with: python3 -m json.tool $outcome" "judgment"
      else
        disp=$(printf '%s\n' "$ofields" | sed -n '1p')
        nfixes=$(printf '%s\n' "$ofields" | sed -n '2p')
        if [[ -n "$disp" ]] && [[ " $dispositions " != *" $disp "* ]]; then
          bad=1; doc_add "debug" "warning" "$outcome" "debugs/$slug: disposition '$disp' is off-enum" \
            "use one of: ${dispositions// / | } — as a bare value; put the why in a separate 'reason' field, not inside the disposition string" "judgment"
        fi
        # the invariant the orchestrator has to *remember* (P6/P7): a declined or
        # relocated job applies nothing, so it graduates no fix.
        if [[ "$disp" == "wont-fix" || "$disp" == "folded-into-request" ]] && [[ "$nfixes" -gt 0 ]]; then
          bad=1; doc_add "debug" "warning" "$outcome" "debugs/$slug: disposition '$disp' but logged_fixes is non-empty ($nfixes)" \
            "a wont-fix/folded job applies nothing — logged_fixes must be [] (Step 3 logs only verified fixes)" "judgment"
        fi
      fi
    fi
  done

  if [[ $job_count -eq 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "debug" "info" "$top_dir" "no debug jobs yet"
    return 0
  fi
  [[ -z "$bad" ]] && doc_add "debug" "pass" "$top_dir" "$job_count debug job(s); spines conform to schema enums + invariants" \
    || { [[ -n "$bad" ]] && doc_add "debug" "info" "$top_dir" "$job_count debug job(s) checked — see warnings above"; }
}

# ── check_vision (v1.38.0+) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Validates first-class pre-request visions plus read-compatible legacy request
# visions. Mechanical --fix remains manifest regeneration only.
check_vision() {
  [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]] || return 0
  local found_any=false vdir slug legacy spine
  local candidates=""
  if [[ -d "$SPEC_VISIONS_DIR" ]]; then
    for vdir in "$SPEC_VISIONS_DIR"/*; do [[ -d "$vdir" ]] && candidates="${candidates}${candidates:+$'\n'}$vdir"; done
  fi
  if [[ -d "$SPEC_REQUESTS_DIR" ]]; then
    for vdir in "$SPEC_REQUESTS_DIR"/*/vision; do [[ -d "$vdir" ]] && candidates="${candidates}${candidates:+$'\n'}$vdir"; done
  fi

  while IFS= read -r vdir; do
    [[ -n "$vdir" ]] || continue
    found_any=true; legacy=false
    _vision_is_legacy "$vdir" && legacy=true
    if $legacy; then slug=$(basename "$(dirname "$vdir")"); else slug=$(basename "$vdir"); fi
    spine="$vdir/VISION.md"
    if [[ ! -f "$spine" ]]; then
      doc_add "vision" "warning" "$vdir" "Vision has no VISION.md spine" "restore the spine or start a new Vision" "judgment"
      continue
    fi

    local status="legacy" missing_sections="" heading
    if ! $legacy; then
      status=$(fm_get "$spine" status)
      case "$status" in draft|proposed|approved|rejected) ;; *) doc_add "vision" "warning" "$spine" "invalid Vision status: ${status:-missing}" "use draft|proposed|approved|rejected" "judgment" ;; esac
      for heading in Intent "North star" Understanding "Experience signature" "Strategies considered" "Chosen direction" Boundaries Evidence Manifest Approval; do
        grep -qF "## $heading" "$spine" || missing_sections="${missing_sections:+$missing_sections, }$heading"
      done
      [[ -z "$missing_sections" ]] || doc_add "vision" "warning" "$spine" "missing spine section(s): $missing_sections" "restore the canonical Vision spine headings" "judgment"
    fi

    local frag_count=0 approved_count=0 unresolved_count=0 malformed="" invalid=""
    local f kind caption reaction subdir
    while IFS= read -r f; do
      [[ -n "$f" ]] || continue; frag_count=$((frag_count + 1))
      kind=$(fm_get "$f" kind); caption=$(fm_get "$f" caption); reaction=$(_vision_fragment_reaction "$f")
      if [[ -z "$kind" || -z "$caption" ]]; then malformed="${malformed:+$malformed, }$(basename "$f")"; continue; fi
      if $legacy; then
        subdir=$(basename "$(dirname "$f")")
        case "$kind:$subdir" in story:stories|ui:ui|arch:arch) ;; *) invalid="${invalid:+$invalid, }$(basename "$f")(kind=$kind in $subdir/)" ;; esac
      else
        in_list "$kind" "strategy story flow ui arch prototype" || invalid="${invalid:+$invalid, }$(basename "$f")(kind=$kind)"
        case "$reaction" in approved) approved_count=$((approved_count + 1)) ;; pending|revise) unresolved_count=$((unresolved_count + 1)) ;; rejected|superseded) ;; *) invalid="${invalid:+$invalid, }$(basename "$f")(reaction=$reaction)" ;; esac
      fi
    done < <(_vision_iter_fragments "$vdir")

    doc_add "vision" "pass" "$vdir" "$frag_count fragment(s), $approved_count approved [$slug · $status]"
    [[ -z "$malformed" ]] || doc_add "vision" "warning" "$vdir" "fragments missing kind/caption: $malformed" "fill required fragment frontmatter" "judgment"
    [[ -z "$invalid" ]] || doc_add "vision" "warning" "$vdir" "invalid fragment kind, location, or reaction: $invalid" "use the Vision fragment contract" "judgment"

    local live_manifest fresh_manifest
    live_manifest=$(awk '/^## Manifest$/{inside=1; next} inside && /^## /{exit} inside{print}' "$spine" | awk 'BEGIN{s=0}/./{s=1}s{print}')
    fresh_manifest=$(_vision_manifest_lines "$vdir")
    [[ "$live_manifest" == "$fresh_manifest" ]] || doc_add "vision" "warning" "$vdir" "spine manifest out of date (fragment state changed)" "regenerate the spine manifest" "mechanical"

    if ! $legacy; then
      if [[ "$status" == proposed || "$status" == approved ]]; then
        (( unresolved_count == 0 && approved_count > 0 )) || doc_add "vision" "warning" "$spine" "$status Vision has unresolved/no approved fragments" "resolve reactions before proposing or approving" "judgment"
      fi
      if [[ "$status" == approved ]]; then
        [[ -n "$(fm_get "$spine" approved_by)" && -n "$(fm_get "$spine" approved_at)" ]] || doc_add "vision" "warning" "$spine" "approved Vision lacks approved_by/approved_at" "record explicit human approval provenance" "judgment"
      fi
      if [[ "$status" == rejected ]]; then
        [[ -n "$(fm_get "$spine" rejected_by)" && -n "$(fm_get "$spine" rejection_reason)" ]] || doc_add "vision" "warning" "$spine" "rejected Vision lacks actor/reason" "record rejection provenance" "judgment"
      fi
    fi
  done <<< "$candidates"

  $found_any || doc_add "vision" "info" "$SPEC_VISIONS_DIR/" "no Vision workspaces — opt-in via 'spectacular imagine <slug>'" "skip" "judgment"
}

# ── check_policies (v1.12.0+) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mechanical self-check of the practice layer: POLICY.md present + well-formed
# (every policy block has a check; severities are block|warn; hooks are from the
# known 8), plus the `understand-before-change` gate on any active request
# (PLAN § Understanding filled OR UNDERSTANDING.md present). Judgment checks are
# left to the skill's injection loop.
check_policies() {
  [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]] || return 0
  local pol="$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/POLICY.md"

  if [[ ! -f "$pol" ]]; then
    # check_workspace already emits the mechanical always-set finding that drives
    # --fix re-scaffolding; emit an info here (fix_type=skip) so the repair loop,
    # which matches on $file alone, doesn't re-scaffold POLICY.md twice.
    doc_add "policies" "info" "$pol" "POLICY.md missing — see the 'workspace' always-set finding (re-scaffolds via --fix)" \
      "skip" "judgment"
    return 0
  fi

  if head -1 "$pol" | grep -q '^---$'; then
    doc_add "policies" "pass" "$pol" "POLICY.md present with frontmatter"
  else
    doc_add "policies" "warning" "$pol" "POLICY.md missing frontmatter delimiter" \
      "add a frontmatter block (version, updated, summary)" "judgment"
  fi

  # Structure check: orphan hooks, missing checks, bad severities, dangling principle refs.
  local orphan_hooks="" missing_check="" bad_sev="" dangling_pr="" policy_count=0
  local cur_hook="" cur_id="" seen_check=false cur_is_block=false
  local pr="$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/PRINCIPLES.md"
  local line
  while IFS= read -r line; do
    case "$line" in
      "## @"*)
        local h="${line#\#\# }"
        h="${h%"${h##*[![:space:]]}"}"
        if ! in_list "$h" "$POLICY_VALID_HOOKS"; then
          orphan_hooks="${orphan_hooks:+$orphan_hooks, }$h"
        fi
        cur_hook="$h"
        ;;
      "### "*)
        # close previous policy block — a `check:` is required only for blockers.
        if [[ -n "$cur_id" ]] && $cur_is_block && ! $seen_check; then
          missing_check="${missing_check:+$missing_check, }$cur_id"
        fi
        cur_id="${line#\#\#\# }"; cur_id="${cur_id%"${cur_id##*[![:space:]]}"}"
        policy_count=$((policy_count + 1))
        seen_check=false; cur_is_block=false
        ;;
      "- principle:"*)
        # Flag a principle ref that can't resolve (no PRINCIPLES.md, or no § N).
        local pn="${line#- principle:}"; pn="${pn//[[:space:]]/}"
        if [[ -n "$pn" ]]; then
          if [[ ! -f "$pr" ]] || ! grep -q "^##[[:space:]]\+${pn}\." "$pr" 2>/dev/null; then
            dangling_pr="${dangling_pr:+$dangling_pr, }${cur_id}→P${pn}"
          fi
        fi
        ;;
      "- check:"*) seen_check=true ;;
      "- severity:"*)
        local sv="${line#- severity:}"; sv="${sv#"${sv%%[![:space:]]*}"}"; sv="${sv%"${sv##*[![:space:]]}"}"
        case "$sv" in
          block) cur_is_block=true ;;
          warn)  ;;
          *) bad_sev="${bad_sev:+$bad_sev, }$cur_id=$sv" ;;
        esac
        ;;
    esac
  done < "$pol"
  # close the final block
  if [[ -n "$cur_id" ]] && $cur_is_block && ! $seen_check; then
    missing_check="${missing_check:+$missing_check, }$cur_id"
  fi

  if [[ $policy_count -eq 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "policies" "warning" "$pol" "POLICY.md has no policy blocks (### <id>)" \
      "re-scaffold via 'spectacular doctor --fix' to restore the 8 defaults" "mechanical"
  else
    doc_add "policies" "pass" "$pol" "$policy_count policy block(s) defined"
  fi
  [[ -n "$orphan_hooks" ]] && doc_add "policies" "warning" "$pol" \
    "unknown hook section(s): $orphan_hooks" "use one of: $POLICY_VALID_HOOKS" "judgment"
  [[ -n "$missing_check" ]] && doc_add "policies" "warning" "$pol" \
    "policy block(s) with no 'check:' field: $missing_check" "add a '- check:' line to each" "judgment"
  [[ -n "$bad_sev" ]] && doc_add "policies" "warning" "$pol" \
    "invalid severity value(s): $bad_sev" "severity must be 'block' or 'warn' (or omitted = non-blocking)" "judgment"
  # Dangling principle refs are info, not error — PRINCIPLES.md is optional.
  [[ -n "$dangling_pr" ]] && doc_add "policies" "info" "$pol" \
    "principle ref(s) with no matching PRINCIPLES.md section: $dangling_pr" \
    "scaffold PRINCIPLES.md (e.g. 'spectacular init --with principles') or drop the principle: tag" "judgment"

  # understand-before-change gate: any active request must have Understanding.
  # Mechanical presence-check; the skill enforces at the transition. Honor config:
  # skip the gate entirely when the policy is disabled in the merged contract.
  if _policy_enabled "understand-before-change"; then
    local reqs_dir="$SPEC_REQUESTS_DIR" plan slug status_v
    if [[ -d "$reqs_dir" ]]; then
      for plan in "$reqs_dir"/*/PLAN.md; do
        [[ -f "$plan" ]] || continue
        status_v="$(fm_get "$plan" "status")"
        [[ "$status_v" == "active" ]] || continue
        slug="$(basename "$(dirname "$plan")")"
        if _plan_understanding_filled "$plan"; then
          doc_add "policies" "pass" "$plan" "[$slug] active + Understanding present (understand-before-change satisfied)"
        else
          doc_add "policies" "warning" "$plan" \
            "[$slug] active but no filled '## Understanding' (or UNDERSTANDING.md) — understand-before-change unmet" \
            "fill PLAN § Understanding (How it works now / What changes / What stays the same) or add UNDERSTANDING.md" "judgment"
        fi
      done
    fi
  fi
}

check_decisions() {
  [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]] || return 0
  local decisions="$SPEC_DECISIONS_DIR/index.md"
  local decisions_dir="$SPEC_DECISIONS_DIR"

  if [[ ! -d "$decisions_dir" ]] || [[ ! -f "$decisions" ]]; then
    doc_add "decisions" "warning" "$decisions" "decisions/ index-mode folder or index.md missing" \
      "run 'spectacular decide' to bootstrap the decisions soft-DB" "judgment"
    return 0
  fi

  # Check 1: mode consistency — decisions/index.md must not contain prose blocks
  if [[ -f "$decisions" ]]; then
    if grep -q "^\*\*Context:\*\*\|^\*\*Decision:\*\*\|^\*\*Consequences:\*\*" "$decisions"; then
      doc_add "decisions" "warning" "$decisions" \
        "decisions/index.md contains prose blocks — file is not a pure index" \
        "run 'spectacular decisions migrate' to convert the remaining prose to per-entry files" "judgment"
    else
      doc_add "decisions" "pass" "$decisions" "decisions/index.md is index-only (no prose blocks)"
    fi
  fi

  # Collect index entries: canonical DEC-NNN plus legacy D<N>.
  local -a index_nums=()
  if [[ -f "$decisions" ]]; then
    local line dnum
    while IFS= read -r line; do
      if [[ "$line" =~ ^\-[[:space:]]\*\*(D|DEC-)([0-9]+)\*\* ]]; then
        index_nums+=("$((10#${BASH_REMATCH[2]}))")
      fi
    done < "$decisions"
  fi

  # Collect file entries: canonical DEC-NNN or legacy D<N>.
  local -a file_nums=()
  local f num
  for f in "$decisions_dir"/D*.md; do
    [[ -f "$f" ]] || continue
    num=$(basename "$f" .md)
    if [[ "$num" == DEC-* ]]; then
      num="${num#DEC-}"
    else
      num="${num#D}"
    fi
    num="${num%%-*}"
    [[ "$num" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] && file_nums+=("$((10#$num))")
  done

  local idx_count=${#index_nums[@]}
  local file_count=${#file_nums[@]}

  # Check 2: no orphan index lines (index entry with no corresponding file)
  local orphans=""
  local n
  for n in ${index_nums[@]+"${index_nums[@]}"}; do
    local has_file=false
    local match
    for match in "${decisions_dir}/D${n}"*.md "${decisions_dir}/DEC-$(_canonical_pad "$n")"*.md; do
      [[ -f "$match" ]] && has_file=true && break
    done
    $has_file || orphans="${orphans:+$orphans, }D${n}"
  done
  if [[ -n "$orphans" ]]; then
    doc_add "decisions" "warning" "$decisions_dir" \
      "orphan index line(s) with no file: $orphans" \
      "create the missing decisions/D<N>-<slug>.md files or remove the stale index lines" "judgment"
  else
    (( idx_count > 0 )) && doc_add "decisions" "pass" "$decisions_dir" "all $idx_count index lines have a corresponding file"
  fi

  # Check 3: no stale files (file with no corresponding index line)
  local stale=""
  for n in ${file_nums[@]+"${file_nums[@]}"}; do
    local found=false
    local idx_n
    for idx_n in ${index_nums[@]+"${index_nums[@]}"}; do
      [[ "$n" == "$idx_n" ]] && found=true && break
    done
    $found || stale="${stale:+$stale, }D${n}"
  done
  if [[ -n "$stale" ]]; then
    doc_add "decisions" "warning" "$decisions_dir" \
      "stale file(s) with no index line: $stale" \
      "add a '- **D<N>** — Title — rationale' line to decisions/index.md for each" "judgment"
  else
    (( file_count > 0 )) && doc_add "decisions" "pass" "$decisions_dir" "all $file_count per-entry files have a corresponding index line"
  fi

  # Check 4: numbering — sequential, no gaps, no duplicates
  if [[ $file_count -gt 0 ]]; then
    # Sort numerically
    local sorted_nums
    sorted_nums=$(printf '%s\n' ${file_nums[@]+"${file_nums[@]}"} | sort -n)
    local prev=0 gap="" dup="" seen_list=""
    while IFS= read -r n; do
      # Duplicate check
      if [[ " $seen_list " == *" $n "* ]]; then
        dup="${dup:+$dup, }D${n}"
      fi
      seen_list="$seen_list $n"
      # Gap check
      if (( n > prev + 1 )); then
        local missing_start=$(( prev + 1 ))
        local missing_end=$(( n - 1 ))
        if (( missing_start == missing_end )); then
          gap="${gap:+$gap, }D${missing_start}"
        else
          gap="${gap:+$gap, }D${missing_start}-D${missing_end}"
        fi
      fi
      prev=$n
    done <<< "$sorted_nums"

    if [[ -n "$gap" ]]; then
      doc_add "decisions" "warning" "$decisions_dir" \
        "D-number gap(s) in decisions/: $gap" \
        "either create the missing files or renumber to close the gap" "judgment"
    fi
    if [[ -n "$dup" ]]; then
      doc_add "decisions" "error" "$decisions_dir" \
        "duplicate D-number(s) in decisions/: $dup" \
        "rename files to remove duplicates" "judgment"
    fi
    if [[ -z "$gap" && -z "$dup" ]]; then
      doc_add "decisions" "pass" "$decisions_dir" "D-numbers are sequential with no gaps or duplicates (1–${prev})"
    fi
  fi

  # Check 5: canonical DEC-NNN-<slug>.md or compatible legacy D<N>-<slug>.md.
  local invalid_prefix_count=0 invalid_prefix_files=""
  for f in "$decisions_dir"/D*.md; do
    [[ -f "$f" ]] || continue
    local bname; bname=$(basename "$f")
    if [[ ! "$bname" =~ ^(DEC-[0-9]{3,}|D[0-9]+)-[a-z0-9-]+.md$ ]]; then
      invalid_prefix_count=$((invalid_prefix_count + 1))
      invalid_prefix_files="${invalid_prefix_files:+$invalid_prefix_files, }$bname"
    fi
  done
  if [[ $invalid_prefix_count -gt 0 ]]; then
    doc_add "decisions" "warning" "$decisions_dir" \
      "$invalid_prefix_count decision file(s) missing canonical DEC-NNN-<slug> or legacy D<N>-<slug> prefix: $invalid_prefix_files" \
      "rename through the canonical-ID migration; do not hand-rewrite links" "judgment"
  fi

  for f in "$decisions_dir"/DEC-*.md; do
    [[ -f "$f" ]] || continue
    local decision_status; decision_status=$(fm_get "$f" status)
    case "$decision_status" in verified|superseded) ;; *) doc_add "decisions" "warning" "$f" "invalid decision status: ${decision_status:-missing}" "use verified|superseded; create a new DEC for reversals" "judgment" ;; esac
    [[ "$decision_status" != superseded || -n "$(fm_get "$f" superseded_by)" ]] || doc_add "decisions" "warning" "$f" "superseded decision lacks superseded_by" "link the replacement DEC" "judgment"
  done
}

# ── check_roadmap (v1.23.0+, b18) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Roadmap index-mode integrity + prune nudge. Mirrors check_decisions.
#   - flat mode (no roadmap/ folder): info only, no index checks
#   - index mode: orphan index lines (## Shipped → no file), stale files
#     (roadmap/v*.md → no index line), and a nudge when shipped prose blocks
#     beyond the keep-window are still inline (prunable via `roadmap migrate`).
check_roadmap() {
  [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR" ]] || return 0
  local roadmap="$SPEC_ROADMAPS_DIR/index.md"
  local roadmap_dir="$SPEC_ROADMAPS_DIR"
  [[ -f "$roadmap" ]] || { doc_add "roadmap" "info" "$roadmap" "roadmaps/index.md not present — skipped"; return 0; }

  local invalid_ledger_statuses
  invalid_ledger_statuses=$(awk -F'|' '/^\|[[:space:]]*b[0-9]+[[:space:]]*\|/ { s=$7; gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/, "", s); if (s !~ /^(candidate|planned|active|shipped|cancelled)$/) print s }' "$roadmap" | sort -u | tr '\n' ' ')
  [[ -z "$invalid_ledger_statuses" ]] || doc_add "roadmap" "warning" "$roadmap" "invalid release-ledger status(es): $invalid_ledger_statuses" "use candidate|planned|active|shipped|cancelled" "judgment"

  # Count inline shipped prose blocks: ## v-blocks whose body has **Status:** shipped.
  # On each new ## heading, bank the previous block if it was a shipped v-block.
  local inline_shipped
  inline_shipped=$(awk '
    /^## / {
      if (inv && shipped) c++
      inv = ($0 ~ /^## v[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+/) ? 1 : 0
      shipped = 0
    }
    /^\*\*Status:\*\*[[:space:]]*shipped/ { if (inv) shipped = 1 }
    END { if (inv && shipped) c++; print c+0 }
  ' "$roadmap")

  # Flat mode — no per-version files yet. Only nudge if many shipped blocks sit inline.
  # Flat mode detection: no version files matching v*.md on disk.
  local vfiles=()
  shopt -s nullglob
  for f in "$roadmap_dir"/v*.md; do
    vfiles+=("$f")
  done
  shopt -u nullglob

  if (( ${#vfiles[@]} == 0 )); then
    if (( inline_shipped > ROADMAP_KEEP_DEFAULT )); then
      doc_add "roadmap" "info" "$roadmap" \
        "$inline_shipped shipped prose blocks inline (flat mode) — beyond keep=$ROADMAP_KEEP_DEFAULT" \
        "run 'spectacular roadmap migrate' to move older shipped prose into roadmaps/v*.md behind a Shipped index" "judgment"
    else
      doc_add "roadmap" "pass" "$roadmap" "flat mode — $inline_shipped shipped block(s) inline (no roadmaps/v*.md files)"
    fi
    return 0
  fi

  # Index mode. Collect index lines (- vX.Y.Z → roadmaps/vX.Y.Z.md) and files.
  local -a idx_vers file_vers
  local line v
  while IFS= read -r line; do
    if [[ "$line" =~ ^-[[:space:]]+(v[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+)[[:space:]]+.*roadmaps/ ]]; then
      idx_vers+=("${BASH_REMATCH[1]}")
    fi
  done < "$roadmap"
  local f
  for f in "${vfiles[@]}"; do
    v=$(basename "$f" .md)
    file_vers+=("$v")
  done

  # Orphan index lines (index entry, no file).
  local orphans=""
  for v in ${idx_vers[@]+"${idx_vers[@]}"}; do
    [[ -f "${roadmap_dir}/${v}.md" ]] || orphans="${orphans:+$orphans, }$v"
  done
  if [[ -n "$orphans" ]]; then
    doc_add "roadmap" "warning" "$roadmap_dir" "orphan Shipped index line(s) with no file: $orphans" \
      "create the missing roadmaps/<v>.md files or remove the stale index lines" "judgment"
  elif (( ${#idx_vers[@]} > 0 )); then
    doc_add "roadmap" "pass" "$roadmap" "all ${#idx_vers[@]} Shipped index line(s) have a corresponding file"
  fi

  # Stale files (file, no index line). Build a padded set of index versions.
  local idx_set=" "; for v in ${idx_vers[@]+"${idx_vers[@]}"}; do idx_set+="$v "; done
  local stale=""
  for v in ${file_vers[@]+"${file_vers[@]}"}; do
    [[ "$idx_set" == *" $v "* ]] || stale="${stale:+$stale, }$v"
  done
  if [[ -n "$stale" ]]; then
    doc_add "roadmap" "warning" "$roadmap_dir" "per-version file(s) with no Shipped index line: $stale" \
      "add index lines under '## Shipped' or remove the stale files" "judgment"
  elif (( ${#file_vers[@]} > 0 )); then
    doc_add "roadmap" "pass" "$roadmap_dir" "all ${#file_vers[@]} per-version file(s) are indexed"
  fi

  # Prune nudge: shipped prose beyond keep-window still inline.
  if (( inline_shipped > ROADMAP_KEEP_DEFAULT )); then
    doc_add "roadmap" "info" "$roadmap" \
      "$inline_shipped shipped block(s) still inline — beyond keep=$ROADMAP_KEEP_DEFAULT" \
      "run 'spectacular roadmap migrate' to move the older ones into roadmaps/" "judgment"
  fi
}

check_fixes() {
  [[ -d "$SPEC_FIXES_DIR" ]] || { doc_add "fixes" "info" "$SPEC_FIXES_DIR/" "no fixes corpus yet"; return 0; }
  local f count=0 verified
  for f in "$SPEC_FIXES_DIR"/*.md; do
    [[ -f "$f" ]] || continue; count=$((count + 1)); verified=$(fm_get "$f" verified)
    if [[ -z "$verified" || "$verified" == null ]] || ! grep -q '^## Verified by' "$f"; then
      doc_add "fixes" "warning" "$f" "fix lacks concrete verification evidence" "move incomplete work back to an audit/request or record verified-by" "judgment"
    fi
  done
  (( count > 0 )) && doc_add "fixes" "pass" "$SPEC_FIXES_DIR/" "$count fix record(s) inspected"
}

check_afk() {
  local dir="$SPEC_AFK_DIR/runs" f status active=0 count=0 field id branch
  [[ -d "$dir" ]] || { doc_add "afk" "info" "$dir" "no AFK authorization runs yet"; return 0; }
  for f in "$dir"/*.md; do
    [[ -f "$f" ]] || continue; count=$((count + 1)); status=$(fm_get "$f" status)
    case "$status" in active|gated) active=$((active + 1)) ;; completed|cancelled) ;; *) doc_add "afk" "warning" "$f" "invalid AFK run status: ${status:-missing}" "use active|gated|completed|cancelled" "judgment" ;; esac
    for field in goal allowed_actions hitl_gates started_at; do
      [[ -n "$(fm_get "$f" "$field")" ]] || doc_add "afk" "warning" "$f" "AFK run missing $field" "record the authorization boundary" "judgment"
    done
    if [[ -n "$(fm_get "$f" authority_version)" ]]; then
      [[ "$(fm_get "$f" authority_version)" == 1 ]] || doc_add "afk" "warning" "$f" "unknown AFK authority_version: $(fm_get "$f" authority_version)" "use authority_version: 1 or omit fields for a legacy run" "judgment"
      for field in authorized_by authorized_at session base integration_branch goal_nodes; do
        [[ -n "$(fm_get "$f" "$field")" ]] || doc_add "afk" "warning" "$f" "new-format AFK run missing $field" "record complete authorization evidence" "judgment"
      done
      id=$(fm_get "$f" id); branch=$(fm_get "$f" integration_branch)
      [[ "$branch" == "afk/$id/integration" ]] || doc_add "afk" "warning" "$f" "integration_branch must be afk/$id/integration" "keep task branches as sibling refs under afk/$id/" "judgment"
      if ! awk '
        function check() { if (seen && (!at || !actor || !scope || !rationale || !evidence)) exit 1 }
        /^### E-[0-9][0-9][0-9] — / { check(); seen=1; want++; if ((substr($2,3)+0) != want) exit 1; at=actor=scope=rationale=evidence=0; next }
        seen && /^- at: .+/ { at=1 }
        seen && /^- actor: .+/ { actor=1 }
        seen && /^- scope: .+/ { scope=1 }
        seen && /^- rationale: .+/ { rationale=1 }
        seen && /^- evidence: .+/ { evidence=1 }
        END { check(); if (!seen) exit 1 }
      ' "$f"; then
        doc_add "afk" "warning" "$f" "new-format event log has missing evidence or non-monotonic IDs" "append complete E-001, E-002, ... events through the CLI" "judgment"
      fi
    fi
  done
  (( active <= 1 )) || doc_add "afk" "error" "$dir" "$active AFK runs are active/gated simultaneously" "complete or cancel all but one" "judgment"
  (( count > 0 )) && doc_add "afk" "pass" "$dir" "$count AFK run record(s) inspected"
}

# ── doctor orchestrator ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dispatch a list of area names to their check_<area> functions.
# Single source of truth — adding a new area only requires touching this one case.
run_areas() {
  for area in "$@"; do
    case "$area" in
      skill)       check_skill ;;
      workspace)   check_workspace ;;
      frontmatter) check_frontmatter ;;
      snapshots)   check_snapshots ;;
      links)       check_links ;;
      lifecycle)   check_lifecycle ;;
      kits)        check_kits ;;
      conventions) check_conventions ;;
      specs)       check_specs ;;
      docs)        check_docs ;;
      personas)    check_personas ;;
      memory)      check_memory ;;
      sessions)    check_sessions ;;
      feedback)    check_feedback ;;
      ideas)       check_ideas ;;
      wayfinding)  check_wayfinding ;;
      debug)       check_debug ;;
      fixes)       check_fixes ;;
      afk)         check_afk ;;
      policies)    check_policies ;;
      vision)      check_vision ;;
      decisions)   check_decisions ;;
      roadmap)     check_roadmap ;;
      *)           die "Unknown doctor area: '$area'" ;;
    esac
  done
}

doctor() {
  doctor_parse_args "$@"

  DOC_FINDINGS=""

  local areas_to_run
  if [[ -n "$DOC_OPT_AREA" ]]; then
    areas_to_run="$DOC_OPT_AREA"
  else
    areas_to_run="$DOC_AREAS"
  fi

  run_areas $areas_to_run

  # Apply mechanical fixes if --fix flag set
  if $DOC_OPT_FIX; then
    doctor_apply_mechanical_fixes
    # Re-run detection to refresh state
    DOC_FINDINGS=""
    run_areas $areas_to_run
  fi

  if [[ "$DOC_OPT_FORMAT" == "json" ]]; then
    doctor_emit_json
  else
    doctor_emit_text
  fi

  # Exit code
  if echo "$DOC_FINDINGS" | grep -q "|error|"; then
    exit 2
  elif echo "$DOC_FINDINGS" | grep -q "|warning|"; then
    exit 1
  fi
  exit 0
}

doctor_apply_mechanical_fixes() {
  local applied=0
  # A --fix run is a structural touch — record which version did it. Idempotent;
  # also backfills provenance on legacy (pre-provenance) workspaces.
  stamp_last_touched
  while IFS='|' read -r area sev file msg fix ftype; do
    [[ "$ftype" == "mechanical" ]] || continue
    case "$file" in
      *.gitignore*) ;;  # handled below
    esac

    # Docs frontmatter stub injection (from check_docs)
    # Either missing delimiter OR missing required field.
    if [[ "$area" == "docs" && "$file" == docs/*.md ]]; then
      if [[ "$msg" == *"missing frontmatter delimiter"* ]]; then
        # Prepend a minimal stub; don't try to infer title from H1, leave that to the user
        if [[ -f "$file" ]] && ! head -1 "$file" | grep -q '^---$'; then
          local section_id
          section_id="$(basename "$(dirname "$file")")"
          [[ "$section_id" == "docs" ]] && section_id=""
          local slug
          slug="$(basename "$file" .md)"
          local tmp="${file}.tmp.$$"
          {
            echo "---"
            echo "title: ${slug}"
            echo "description: TODO — one-sentence description"
            echo "section: ${section_id}"
            echo "status: draft"
            echo "updated: ${TODAY}"
            echo "---"
            echo ""
            cat "$file"
          } > "$tmp" && mv "$tmp" "$file"
          echo "  ✓ fixed [docs]: injected frontmatter stub into $file"
          applied=$((applied + 1))
        fi
        continue
      fi
      if [[ "$msg" == *"missing required frontmatter field:"* ]]; then
        # Extract the field name from the message
        local field
        field=$(echo "$msg" | sed -n 's/.*missing required frontmatter field: \([a-z]*\).*/\1/p')
        if [[ -n "$field" && -f "$file" ]]; then
          # Insert "<field>: TODO" after the opening --- line (right at top of frontmatter)
          # Skip if field somehow already present
          local fm
          fm=$(awk '/^---$/ { count++; if (count == 2) exit; next } count == 1' "$file")
          if ! echo "$fm" | grep -qE "^${field}:"; then
            local default_val="TODO"
            [[ "$field" == "status" ]] && default_val="draft"
            [[ "$field" == "updated" ]] && default_val="$TODAY"
            local tmp="${file}.tmp.$$"
            awk -v field="$field" -v val="$default_val" '
              BEGIN { inserted=0; count=0 }
              /^---$/ { count++; print; if (count == 1 && !inserted) { print field ": " val; inserted=1 }; next }
              { print }
            ' "$file" > "$tmp" && mv "$tmp" "$file"
            echo "  ✓ fixed [docs]: injected '${field}: ${default_val}' into $file"
            applied=$((applied + 1))
          fi
        fi
        continue
      fi
    fi

    # Legacy numbered PLAN headings → unnumbered canonical form (lifecycle area).
    # "## 1. Goal" → "## Goal", etc. Only the 7 canonical section names, so a
    # numbered heading that isn't a required section is left untouched.
    if [[ "$area" == "lifecycle" && "$msg" == *"legacy numbered section headings"* ]]; then
      if [[ -f "$file" ]]; then
        local tmp="${file}.tmp.$$"
        sed -E 's/^## [0-9]+\. (Goal|Constraints|Milestones|Tasks|Dependencies|Validation|Deliverables)$/## \1/' \
          "$file" > "$tmp" && mv "$tmp" "$file"
        echo "  ✓ fixed [lifecycle]: de-numbered PLAN section headings in $file"
        applied=$((applied + 1))
      fi
      continue
    fi

    # Pack-driven gitignore drift (from check_conventions in scaffold/enforce modes)
    # Findings have area=conventions and msg containing "requires gitignore entry: 'X'"
    if [[ "$area" == "conventions" && "$msg" == *"gitignore entry:"* ]]; then
      # Extract the entry between single quotes: ...entry: 'X' (...
      local entry
      entry=$(echo "$msg" | sed -n "s/.*gitignore entry: '\([^']*\)'.*/\1/p")
      if [[ -n "$entry" ]]; then
        [[ -f ".gitignore" ]] || touch .gitignore
        if ! grep -qF -- "$entry" .gitignore; then
          echo "$entry" >> .gitignore
          echo "  ✓ fixed [conventions]: appended $entry to .gitignore"
          applied=$((applied + 1))
        fi
      fi
      continue
    fi

    # Vision spine manifest drift (from check_vision)
    if [[ "$area" == "vision" && "$msg" == *"spine manifest out of date"* ]]; then
      # $file is the vision/ dir
      if [[ -d "$file" ]]; then
        _regen_vision_manifest "$file"
        echo "  ✓ fixed [vision]: regenerated spine manifest in $file"
        applied=$((applied + 1))
      fi
      continue
    fi

    # gitignore append (workspace area — .spectacular.local/ baseline)
    # Skip snapshots-area gitignore findings — the snapshots block below owns those.
    if [[ "$area" != "snapshots" ]] && [[ "$file" == ".gitignore"* || "$msg" == *".gitignore"* ]]; then
      if [[ -f ".gitignore" ]]; then
        if ! grep -qF ".spectacular.local/" .gitignore; then
          echo ".spectacular.local/" >> .gitignore
          echo "  ✓ fixed [gitignore]: appended .spectacular.local/"
          applied=$((applied + 1))
        fi
      else
        echo ".spectacular.local/" > .gitignore
        echo "  ✓ fixed [gitignore]: created with .spectacular.local/"
        applied=$((applied + 1))
      fi
      continue
    fi

    # Missing dir
    if [[ "$file" == "$SPEC_REQUESTS_DIR/" || "$file" == "$SPEC_SPECS_DIR/" ]]; then
      mkdir -p "$file"
      [[ "$file" == "$SPEC_SPECS_DIR/" ]] && touch "${file}.gitkeep"
      echo "  ✓ fixed [workspace]: created $file"
      applied=$((applied + 1))
      continue
    fi

    # Legacy current/ → specs/ migration (specs area, mechanical)
    if [[ "$area" == "specs" && "$msg" == *"legacy current/ folder"* ]]; then
      if [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/current" && ! -d "$SPEC_SPECS_DIR" ]]; then
        mv "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/current" "$SPEC_SPECS_DIR"
        echo "  ✓ fixed [specs]: renamed .spectacular/current/ → .spectacular/specs/"
        applied=$((applied + 1))
      fi
      continue
    fi

    # Legacy snapshot migration (snapshots area, mechanical)
    # Pattern: .spectacular/<DOC>@v<N>.md → <store>/<DOC>/@v<N>.md
    if [[ "$area" == "snapshots" && "$msg" == *"legacy root-level snapshot"* ]]; then
      if [[ -f "$file" ]]; then
        local b doc_prefix ver_part target_dir target snap_root
        snap_root="$(snapshot_store_root)"
        b=$(basename "$file")
        doc_prefix="${b%@v*}"
        ver_part="@v${b#*@v}"
        target_dir="${snap_root}/${doc_prefix}"
        target="${target_dir}/${ver_part}"
        mkdir -p "$target_dir"
        # Prefer git mv when the file is tracked; fall back to plain mv
        if git ls-files --error-unmatch "$file" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
          git mv "$file" "$target" 2>/dev/null && {
            echo "  ✓ fixed [snapshots]: git mv $file → $target"
            applied=$((applied + 1))
          }
        else
          mv "$file" "$target" && {
            echo "  ✓ fixed [snapshots]: mv $file → $target"
            applied=$((applied + 1))
          }
        fi
      fi
      continue
    fi

    # gitignore drift for the snapshot store (b16, mechanical)
    if [[ "$area" == "snapshots" && "$msg" == *"snapshots.gitignore"* ]]; then
      if snapshot_gitignore_sync; then
        echo "  ✓ fixed [snapshots]: synced .gitignore to snapshots.gitignore=$(config_snapshots_gitignore)"
        applied=$((applied + 1))
      fi
      continue
    fi

    # Folder rename: snapshots/ → <configured folder> (b16, mechanical)
    if [[ "$area" == "snapshots" && "$msg" == *"config wants"* ]]; then
      local snap_folder
      snap_folder="$(config_snapshots_folder)"
      if [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/snapshots" && ! -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/$snap_folder" ]]; then
        if git ls-files --error-unmatch "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/snapshots" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
          git mv "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/snapshots" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/$snap_folder" 2>/dev/null && {
            echo "  ✓ fixed [snapshots]: git mv snapshots/ → ${snap_folder}/"
            applied=$((applied + 1)); }
        else
          mv "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/snapshots" "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/$snap_folder" && {
            echo "  ✓ fixed [snapshots]: mv snapshots/ → ${snap_folder}/"
            applied=$((applied + 1)); }
        fi
      fi
      continue
    fi

    # Dangling symlink
    if [[ "$sev" == "error" && "$file" == *".claude/skills/spectacular"* ]]; then
      local agents_dir
      agents_dir="$(agents_skill_dir)"
      if [[ -d "$agents_dir" ]]; then
        rm -f "$file"
        mkdir -p "$(dirname "$file")"
        ln -s "$agents_dir" "$file"
        echo "  ✓ fixed [skill]: recreated symlink $file → $agents_dir"
        applied=$((applied + 1))
      fi
      continue
    fi

    # Missing always-set or index file → re-scaffold using doc_<id>
    if [[ "$file" == "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/PRD.md" || "$file" == "$SPEC_SPECS_DIR/index.md" || "$file" == "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/config.yaml" || "$file" == "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/POLICY.md" || "$file" == "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/AGENTS.md" || "$file" == "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/CLAUDE.md" || "$file" == "$SPEC_ROADMAPS_DIR/index.md" || "$file" == "$SPEC_DECISIONS_DIR/index.md" || "$file" == "$SPEC_MEMORIES_DIR/index.md" || "$file" == "$SPEC_SESSIONS_DIR/index.md" ]]; then
      local fname fdir name
      fname=$(basename "$file")
      fdir=$(basename "$(dirname "$file")")
      name="${OPT_NAME:-$(slug_from_dir)}"
      if [[ "$fname" == "index.md" ]]; then
        case "$fdir" in
          specs)     doc_spec "$name" ;;
          roadmaps)  doc_roadmap "$name" ;;
          decisions) doc_decisions ;;
          memories)  doc_memory ;;
          sessions)  doc_sessions ;;
        esac
      else
        case "$fname" in
          PRD.md)        doc_prd "$name" "blank" ;;
          config.yaml)   doc_config "$name" "" "AGENTS.md" "blank" ;;
          POLICY.md)     doc_policy "$name" ;;
          AGENTS.md|CLAUDE.md) doc_agents "$name" "$fname" ;;
        esac
      fi
      echo "  ✓ fixed [workspace]: re-scaffolded $file"
      applied=$((applied + 1))
      continue
    fi
  done <<< "$DOC_FINDINGS"

  if [[ $applied -eq 0 ]]; then
    echo "  (no mechanical fixes applied)"
  fi
  echo ""
}

# ── text emitter ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
doctor_emit_text() {
  echo "Spectacular doctor"
  echo ""

  local last_area="" errors=0 warnings=0 infos=0 nonpass=""
  while IFS='|' read -r area sev file msg fix ftype; do
    [[ -z "$area" ]] && continue
    if [[ "$area" != "$last_area" ]]; then
      last_area="$area"
    fi
    case "$sev" in
      pass)    icon="✅" ;;
      warning) icon="⚠️ "; warnings=$((warnings + 1)) ;;
      error)   icon="❌"; errors=$((errors + 1)) ;;
      info)    icon="ℹ️ "; infos=$((infos + 1)) ;;
      *)       icon="?"  ;;
    esac
    printf "%-13s %s %s — %s\n" "$area" "$icon" "$file" "$msg"
    if [[ -n "$fix" && "$sev" != "pass" ]]; then
      local route="(mechanical — \`--fix\` applies)"
      [[ "$ftype" == "judgment" ]] && route="(judgment — \`/spectacular doctor --fix\`)"
      printf "%-13s    → %s %s\n" "" "$fix" "$route"
    fi
    # Collect non-pass rows compactly for the findings block below — a long run
    # of pass rows otherwise drowns them mid-report. Only real severities: a
    # multi-line finding message parses as stray continuation rows — skip those.
    case "$sev" in
      warning|error|info)
        nonpass+="$(printf "%s %s · %s — %s%s" "$icon" "$area" "$file" "$msg" "${fix:+ → $fix}")"$'\n' ;;
    esac
  done <<< "$DOC_FINDINGS"

  echo ""
  printf "%d error(s), %d warning(s), %d info\n" "$errors" "$warnings" "$infos"
  if [[ -n "$nonpass" ]]; then
    echo ""
    echo "── findings ──"
    printf "%s" "$nonpass"
  fi
  if [[ $errors -gt 0 || $warnings -gt 0 ]]; then
    echo ""
    echo "Run \`spectacular doctor --fix\` for mechanical repairs."
    echo "Run \`/spectacular doctor --fix\` (in your AI agent) for judgment repairs."
  fi
}

# ── json emitter ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
doctor_emit_json() {
  local ran_at
  ran_at="$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
  local workspace="$(pwd)"
  local errors=0 warnings=0 infos=0 first=true

  printf '{\n'
  printf '  "version": "0.3.0",\n'
  printf '  "ran_at": "%s",\n' "$ran_at"
  printf '  "workspace": "%s",\n' "$workspace"
  printf '  "findings": [\n'

  while IFS='|' read -r area sev file msg fix ftype; do
    [[ -z "$area" ]] && continue
    [[ "$sev" == "pass" ]] && continue  # pass entries omitted from json (signal-to-noise)
    case "$sev" in
      warning) warnings=$((warnings + 1)) ;;
      error)   errors=$((errors + 1)) ;;
      info)    infos=$((infos + 1)) ;;
    esac
    if ! $first; then printf ',\n'; fi
    first=false
    # JSON-escape strings (basic — escape quotes and backslashes)
    local esc_msg="${msg//\\/\\\\}"; esc_msg="${esc_msg//\"/\\\"}"
    local esc_fix="${fix//\\/\\\\}"; esc_fix="${esc_fix//\"/\\\"}"
    local esc_file="${file//\\/\\\\}"; esc_file="${esc_file//\"/\\\"}"
    printf '    {"area": "%s", "severity": "%s", "file": "%s", "message": "%s", "proposed_fix": "%s", "fix_type": "%s"}' \
      "$area" "$sev" "$esc_file" "$esc_msg" "$esc_fix" "$ftype"
  done <<< "$DOC_FINDINGS"

  printf '\n  ],\n'
  printf '  "summary": { "errors": %d, "warnings": %d, "info": %d }\n' "$errors" "$warnings" "$infos"
  printf '}\n'
}

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# pack subcommand — convention-pack lifecycle (install / list / remove)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

pack_usage() {
  cat <<EOF
Usage: spectacular pack <verb> [args]

Manage convention packs — repo-shape opinions (naming + taxonomy + gitignore
+ file-placement + project-types). Schema: skills/spectacular/references/packs-contract.md

Verbs:
  list                       Show installed packs across all scopes
  install <name> [--from <path>]
                             Install pack to ~/.spectacular/packs/<name>/.
                             --from <path> copies from a local folder (default:
                             searches bundled, then app-store at <repo>/packs/<name>).
  remove <name> [--force]    Remove user-scope pack at ~/.spectacular/packs/<name>/.
                             --force allows removing bundled/project-local packs.
  show <name>                Print pack.md frontmatter for the named pack.

Pack scopes (precedence: project-local > user > app-store > bundled):
  bundled        skills/spectacular/templates/packs/<name>/
  app-store      <repo-root>/packs/<name>/
  user           ~/.spectacular/packs/<name>/
  project-local  <project>/.spectacular/packs/<name>/

Examples:
  spectacular pack list
  spectacular pack install minimal
  spectacular pack install alex-default --from /path/to/pack
  spectacular pack show minimal
  spectacular pack remove old-pack
EOF
}

pack_user_dir() { echo "${HOME}/.spectacular/packs"; }

pack_bundled_dir() {
  local agents_dir
  agents_dir="$(agents_skill_dir)"
  echo "${agents_dir}/templates/packs"
}

pack_appstore_dir() {
  # Walk up from cli/ looking for a packs/ sibling (source repo layout)
  # Fallback: cwd/packs if present
  local candidate
  if [[ -d "${SCRIPT_DIR}/../packs" ]]; then
    candidate="$(cd "${SCRIPT_DIR}/.." && pwd)/packs"
    echo "$candidate"
  elif [[ -d "./packs" ]]; then
    echo "$(pwd)/packs"
  else
    echo ""
  fi
}

pack_projectlocal_dir() {
  if [[ -d "$SPEC_WORKSPACE_DIR/packs" ]]; then
    echo "$(pwd)/.spectacular/packs"
  else
    echo ""
  fi
}

# Resolve a pack name to a source folder, applying precedence rules.
# Args: $1 = pack name, $2 = optional explicit source override (--from)
# Stdout: absolute path to the resolved pack folder, or empty if not found
pack_resolve() {
  local name="$1"
  local override="${2:-}"

  if [[ -n "$override" ]]; then
    [[ -d "$override" ]] && echo "$override" && return 0
    return 1
  fi

  # Precedence order for INSTALL source (read from): project-local → user → app-store → bundled
  local pl ud as bd
  pl="$(pack_projectlocal_dir)"
  ud="$(pack_user_dir)"
  as="$(pack_appstore_dir)"
  bd="$(pack_bundled_dir)"

  for dir in "$pl" "$ud" "$as" "$bd"; do
    [[ -z "$dir" ]] && continue
    if [[ -d "${dir}/${name}" && -f "${dir}/${name}/pack.md" ]]; then
      echo "${dir}/${name}"
      return 0
    fi
  done
  return 1
}

pack_scope_of() {
  local path="$1"
  local pl ud as bd
  pl="$(pack_projectlocal_dir)"
  ud="$(pack_user_dir)"
  as="$(pack_appstore_dir)"
  bd="$(pack_bundled_dir)"

  # Order matters: most-specific scope first. Empty scope dirs are skipped
  # (an empty $pl would otherwise expand the pattern to "/*" and match everything).
  [[ -n "$pl" && "$path" == "${pl}/"* ]] && echo "project-local" && return
  [[ -n "$ud" && "$path" == "${ud}/"* ]] && echo "user" && return
  [[ -n "$as" && "$path" == "${as}/"* ]] && echo "app-store" && return
  [[ -n "$bd" && "$path" == "${bd}/"* ]] && echo "bundled" && return
  echo "unknown"
}

pack_list() {
  echo "Convention packs:"
  echo ""
  local found=0
  for scope_pair in \
    "bundled|$(pack_bundled_dir)" \
    "app-store|$(pack_appstore_dir)" \
    "user|$(pack_user_dir)" \
    "project-local|$(pack_projectlocal_dir)"
  do
    local scope="${scope_pair%%|*}"
    local dir="${scope_pair##*|}"
    [[ -z "$dir" || ! -d "$dir" ]] && continue
    local entries=()
    for sub in "$dir"/*/; do
      [[ -d "$sub" ]] || continue
      local name
      name="$(basename "$sub")"
      [[ -f "${sub}pack.md" ]] || continue
      entries+=("$name")
      found=$((found + 1))
    done
    if [[ ${#entries[@]} -gt 0 ]]; then
      printf "  %-14s %s\n" "[${scope}]" "$dir"
      for e in "${entries[@]}"; do
        printf "    • %s\n" "$e"
      done
    fi
  done
  echo ""
  if [[ $found -eq 0 ]]; then
    echo "  (no packs found)"
  else
    echo "Install: spectacular pack install <name>"
    echo "Show:    spectacular pack show <name>"
  fi
}

pack_install() {
  local name="$1"
  local from_path="${2:-}"
  [[ -z "$name" ]] && die "pack install: missing pack name. Usage: spectacular pack install <name> [--from <path>]"

  local src
  if ! src="$(pack_resolve "$name" "$from_path")"; then
    if [[ -n "$from_path" ]]; then
      die "pack install: source path not found or not a pack folder: $from_path"
    fi
    die "pack install: pack '$name' not found. Run 'spectacular pack list' to see available packs."
  fi

  local user_dir
  user_dir="$(pack_user_dir)"
  mkdir -p "$user_dir"
  local dest="${user_dir}/${name}"

  if [[ -d "$dest" ]]; then
    die "pack install: '$name' already installed at $dest. Remove first: spectacular pack remove $name"
  fi

  # Copy via cp -R (POSIX-portable enough; preserves dotfiles like templates/.gitignore)
  cp -R "$src" "$dest"

  echo "✓ installed $name → $dest"
  echo "  source:  $src ($(pack_scope_of "$src"))"
  echo ""
  echo "Activate per-repo by adding to .spectacular/config.yaml:"
  echo "  convention_pack:"
  echo "    source: $name"
  echo "    mode: suggest    # or scaffold | enforce"
}

pack_remove() {
  local name="$1"
  local force="${2:-false}"
  [[ -z "$name" ]] && die "pack remove: missing pack name. Usage: spectacular pack remove <name> [--force]"

  local user_dir
  user_dir="$(pack_user_dir)"
  local target="${user_dir}/${name}"

  if [[ -d "$target" ]]; then
    rm -rf "$target"
    echo "✓ removed user-scope pack: $target"
    return 0
  fi

  # If not in user scope, check if it exists elsewhere — refuse without --force
  local found
  if found="$(pack_resolve "$name")"; then
    local scope
    scope="$(pack_scope_of "$found")"
    if [[ "$force" != "true" ]]; then
      die "pack remove: '$name' lives in $scope scope ($found). Use --force to remove."
    fi
    rm -rf "$found"
    echo "✓ removed $scope pack: $found"
    return 0
  fi

  die "pack remove: '$name' not installed in any scope."
}

pack_show() {
  local name="$1"
  [[ -z "$name" ]] && die "pack show: missing pack name. Usage: spectacular pack show <name>"

  local src
  if ! src="$(pack_resolve "$name")"; then
    die "pack show: '$name' not found in any scope."
  fi

  local manifest="${src}/pack.md"
  [[ -f "$manifest" ]] || die "pack show: $manifest missing"

  echo "pack:   $name"
  echo "scope:  $(pack_scope_of "$src")"
  echo "path:   $src"
  echo ""
  echo "── pack.md frontmatter ──"
  awk '/^---$/{c++; if(c==2) exit; if(c==1) next} c==1' "$manifest"
}

pack() {
  local verb="${1:-}"
  case "$verb" in
    ""|--help|-h) pack_usage; exit 0 ;;
    # Skill verbs (v1.19.0+): pack authoring (new/grill/refine/review) needs an
    # LLM — redirect to the skill. The CLI owns only the mechanical lifecycle
    # (list/install/remove/show). Matches the `<doc> grill` redirect pattern.
    new|grill|refine|review)
      shift
      skill_verb_message "pack $verb" \
        "Agentic pack authoring — interview/rewrite/gate-check a convention pack (doc-id: pack)." \
        "$@"
      ;;
    list)
      pack_list
      ;;
    install)
      shift
      local name="${1:-}"
      [[ -n "$name" && "$name" != -* ]] || die "pack install: missing pack name. Usage: spectacular pack install <name> [--from <path>]"
      shift || true
      local from_path=""
      while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do
        case "$1" in
          --from) require_value "--from" "${2:-}"; from_path="$2"; shift 2 ;;
          *) die "pack install: unknown option: $1" ;;
        esac
      done
      pack_install "$name" "$from_path"
      ;;
    remove)
      shift
      local name="${1:-}"
      [[ -n "$name" && "$name" != -* ]] || die "pack remove: missing pack name. Usage: spectacular pack remove <name> [--force]"
      shift || true
      local force="false"
      while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do
        case "$1" in
          --force) force="true"; shift ;;
          *) die "pack remove: unknown option: $1" ;;
        esac
      done
      pack_remove "$name" "$force"
      ;;
    show)
      shift
      pack_show "${1:-}"
      ;;
    *)
      die "Unknown pack verb: '$verb'. Run 'spectacular pack --help' for usage."
      ;;
  esac
}

# ── skill-verb stubs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These verbs are interactive flows owned by the skill (not the CLI). Their
# references in docs/SKILL/refs use the `spectacular <verb>` form, so when a
# user types one directly we explain rather than emit "Unknown command".

skill_verb_message() {
  local verb="$1"; shift
  local description="$1"; shift
  cat >&2 <<EOF
'spectacular $verb' is an interactive skill flow — it must run inside your AI agent.

  ${description}

Run it as:  /spectacular $verb${1:+ }$*

(Inside Claude Code, Codex, etc. with the spectacular skill installed.)
EOF
  exit 1
}

main() {
  local subcmd="${1:-}"

  case "$subcmd" in
    --version|-v|version)
      echo "spectacular ${SPECTACULAR_VERSION}"
      exit 0
      ;;
    ""|--help|-h|help)
      top_usage; exit 0
      ;;
  esac

  if schema_write_gate_required "$@"; then
    require_supported_workspace_schema_for_write
  fi

  # Skill-owned interactive verbs — explain and exit, don't pretend to dispatch.
  # Exception: `status --against-latest` is a CLI-mechanical flag (no skill needed).
  case "$subcmd" in
    act)
      shift
      [[ -n "${1:-}" ]] || die "Usage: /spectacular act <SPC-ID>"
      local _act_path _act_id
      _act_path=$(_spec_find "$1") || die "act: specification '$1' not found"
      _act_id=$(fm_get "$_act_path" id)
      [[ "$(fm_get "$_act_path" status)" == approved ]] || die "act: $_act_id is not approved; implementation is not authorized"
      shift
      skill_verb_message "act $_act_id" \
        "Authorize and begin implementation from an approved specification: resolve one request, run gates, record provenance, compile its brief, and initialize native agent planning." \
        "$@"
      ;;
    grill|refine|review)
      local _conversation_verb="$subcmd"
      shift
      [[ -n "${1:-}" ]] || die "Usage: /spectacular $_conversation_verb <document> [target]"
      local _conversation_doc="$1"; shift
      in_list "$_conversation_doc" "$KNOWN_DOCS" || die "$_conversation_verb: unknown document '$_conversation_doc'"
      skill_verb_message "$_conversation_verb $_conversation_doc" \
        "Agentic document workflow — resolved target: $_conversation_doc${1:+ ($*)}." \
        "$@"
      ;;
    archive)  shift; cmd_archive "$@"; exit $? ;;
    status)
      shift
      # Intercept CLI-mechanical flags/args before falling through to the skill stub.
      local _status_brief=false _status_json=false
      local _i=0
      while (( _i < $# )); do
        _i=$((_i + 1))
        local arg="${!_i}"
        case "$arg" in
          --against-latest) cmd_status_against_latest; exit $? ;;
          --since)
            local _next=$((_i + 1))
            cmd_status_since "${!_next:-}"
            exit $?
            ;;
          --since=*)
            cmd_status_since "${arg#--since=}"
            exit $?
            ;;
          --brief) _status_brief=true ;;
          --json) _status_json=true ;;
        esac
      done
      if $_status_brief; then
        # `--brief` has no positional form; it is a bounded orientation view.
        for arg in "$@"; do
          case "$arg" in --brief|--json) ;; *) die "status --brief: unknown argument '$arg'" ;; esac; done
        cmd_status_brief "$_status_json"; exit $?
      fi
      if $_status_json; then cmd_status_json; exit $?; fi
      # Positional: bare `status` → fleet table; `status <slug>` → request card.
      if [[ $# -eq 0 ]]; then
        cmd_status_fleet; exit $?
      elif [[ $# -eq 1 && "$1" != -* ]]; then
        cmd_status_card "$1"; exit $?
      fi
      skill_verb_message "status" "Briefing of project state — frontmatter only, no full-file reads." "$@"
      ;;
    new)      shift; cmd_new "$@"; exit $? ;;
    snapshot)
      shift
      if [[ "${1:-}" == "prune" ]]; then shift; cmd_snapshot_prune "$@"; else cmd_snapshot "$@"; fi
      exit $? ;;
    remember)
      shift
      # v1.5.0: if invoked with text argument, route to CLI writer.
      # Bare `spectacular remember` (or `remember this`) remains a skill verb.
      if [[ $# -eq 0 ]] || [[ "$1" == "this" && $# -eq 1 ]]; then
        skill_verb_message "remember" "Write an operational lesson to .spectacular/memory/." "$@"
      else
        cmd_remember "$@"; exit $?
      fi
      ;;
    decide)   shift; cmd_decide "$@"; exit $? ;;
    docs-impact) shift; cmd_docs_impact "$@"; exit $? ;;
    session)  shift; cmd_session "$@"; exit $? ;;
    # Lifecycle advance (v1.19.0+): `advance` is canonical; `promote` is a
    # deprecation alias (warns once, then runs). Renamed from `promote` to free
    # the word for `idea promote` and read as a clear forward-gear verb.
    advance)  shift; cmd_promote "$@"; exit $? ;;
    promote)
      shift
      warn "'spectacular promote' is deprecated — use 'spectacular advance'. (alias still works)"
      cmd_promote "$@"; exit $? ;;
    # Undo (v1.22.0+): reverse the last lifecycle mutation via .last-mutation breadcrumb.
    undo)     shift; cmd_undo "$@"; exit $? ;;
    # Verify (v1.11.0+): skill-only validation walk. Needs an LLM to read each
    # check, run/judge it by kind, and gate review→verified. No CLI dispatch.
    verify)
      shift
      skill_verb_message "verify" \
        "Validation walk — reads VERIFY.md (or PLAN § Validation), verifies each check by its kind (executable / assertable / judgable / observable / manual), records to VERIFY-LOG, and gates review→verified." \
        "$@"
      ;;
    # Sweep (v1.35.0+): skill-only fleet audit. Dispatches request-auditor
    # subagents (review + ticked-active deep, planned batched overlap check),
    # persists findings to VERIFY-LOG + SESSION.md. Never promotes.
    sweep)
      shift
      skill_verb_message "sweep" \
        "Review sweep — read-only audit of the request fleet: cross-checks each review/ticked-active request's claims vs code/tests/evidence via request-auditor subagents, quick-checks planned requests for overlap with shipped work, appends sweep entries to VERIFY-LOG, hands off via SESSION.md. Never promotes — feeds the verify walk." \
        "$@"
      ;;
    # Feedback (v1.6.0+; renamed from feedback-loop in v1.19.0): post-build
    # learning. `experiment` is intentionally not an alias: route that word by
    # uncertainty (research, spike, Vision prototype, or feedback).
    feedback|feedback-loop|iterate|test|probe|try)
      shift; cmd_feedback_loop "$@"; exit $? ;;
    # Idea (v1.7.0+): thinking scratchpad.
    idea)
      shift; cmd_idea "$@"; exit $? ;;
    question)
      shift; cmd_question "$@"; exit $? ;;
    research)
      shift; cmd_discovery_record research research RES "$@"; exit $? ;;
    spike)
      shift; cmd_discovery_record spike spikes SPK "$@"; exit $? ;;
    spec)
      case "${2:-}" in
        new|list|approve|confirm|act|implement|deprecate|archive) shift; cmd_spec_record "$@"; exit $? ;;
        ""|grill|refine|review) : ;;
        *) shift; cmd_spec_record "$@"; exit $? ;;
      esac
      ;;
    wayfind)
      shift; cmd_wayfind "$@"; exit $? ;;
    afk)
      shift; cmd_afk "$@"; exit $? ;;
    workspace)
      shift; cmd_workspace "$@"; exit $? ;;
    github)
      shift; cmd_github "$@"; exit $? ;;
    id)
      shift; cmd_id "$@"; exit $? ;;
    collections)
      shift; cmd_collections "$@"; exit $? ;;
    lifecycle)
      shift; cmd_lifecycle_migrate "$@"; exit $? ;;
    # Audit / fix (v1.25.0+): bug-lifecycle soft-DB collections.
    audit)
      shift; cmd_audit "$@"; exit $? ;;
    fix)
      shift; cmd_fix "$@"; exit $? ;;
    # Imagine / Vision (v1.38.0+): pre-request direction discovery.
    imagine)
      shift
      if [[ $# -eq 0 ]]; then
        skill_verb_message "imagine" \
          "Pre-request direction discovery — Understand current reality, imagine proportional fragments, probe uncertainty, gather human reactions, confirm Vision, then derive a draft SPC." \
          "$@"
      else
        cmd_imagine "$@"; exit $?
      fi
      ;;
    vision)
      shift; cmd_vision "$@"; exit $? ;;
    # next (v1.19.0+): read-only single-next-action pointer.
    next)       shift; cmd_next "$@";       exit $? ;;
    # Read verbs (v1.8.0+): plural-noun = list, singular-noun = detail.
    requests)   shift; cmd_requests "$@";   exit $? ;;
    decisions)  shift; cmd_decisions "$@";  exit $? ;;
    memories)   shift; cmd_memories "$@";   exit $? ;;
    sessions)   shift; cmd_sessions "$@";   exit $? ;;
    request)    shift; cmd_request "$@";    exit $? ;;
    links)      shift; cmd_links "$@";      exit $? ;;
    traffic)    shift; cmd_traffic "$@";    exit $? ;;
    decision)   shift; cmd_decision "$@";   exit $? ;;
    memory)     shift; cmd_memory "$@";     exit $? ;;
    show)       shift; cmd_show "$@";       exit $? ;;
    summary)    shift; cmd_summary "$@";    exit $? ;;
    progress)   shift; cmd_progress "$@";   exit $? ;;
    roadmap)    shift; cmd_roadmap "$@";    exit $? ;;
    paths)      shift; cmd_paths "$@";      exit $? ;;
    # Policy (v1.12.0+): read the merged policy contract. CLI-mechanical
    # retrieval — the skill calls `policy @<hook>` on entering a phase.
    # `policy grill|refine|review` falls through to the doc-verb redirect
    # (POLICY is also a doc); everything else is CLI retrieval.
    policy)
      case "${2:-}" in
        grill|refine|review) : ;;  # fall through to doc-verb pre-check below
        *) shift; cmd_policy "$@"; exit $? ;;
      esac
      ;;
  esac

  # An SPC identifier is unambiguous in conversational use, so the shortest
  # form is an alias for `/spectacular act SPC-NNN`.
  if [[ "$subcmd" =~ ^(SPC|spc|SPEC|spec|S|s)-?[0-9]+$ ]]; then
    local _bare_path _bare_id
    _bare_path=$(_spec_find "$subcmd") || die "act: specification '$subcmd' not found"
    _bare_id=$(fm_get "$_bare_path" id)
    [[ "$(fm_get "$_bare_path" status)" == approved ]] || die "act: $_bare_id is not approved; implementation is not authorized"
    shift
    skill_verb_message "act $_bare_id" \
      "Authorize and begin implementation from this approved specification; the bare SPC form is unambiguous." \
      "$@"
  fi

  if [[ "$subcmd" == "doctor" ]]; then
    shift
    doctor "$@"
    exit $?
  fi

  if [[ "$subcmd" == "pack" ]]; then
    shift
    pack "$@"
    exit 0
  fi

  if [[ "$subcmd" == "migrate" ]]; then
    shift
    cmd_migrate "$@"
    exit $?
  fi

  if [[ "$subcmd" == "touch" ]]; then
    shift
    cmd_touch "$@"
    exit $?
  fi

  # ── doc-verb pre-check (agentic verbs are skill-only) ──
  # Matches `spectacular <doc> grill|refine|review` and redirects when called
  # from terminal. Grill + refine require an LLM (slot interview, vibe→spec
  # rewrite). Review is mixed — structural part runs in `doctor`, semantic
  # part requires the skill.
  if in_list "$subcmd" "$KNOWN_DOCS"; then
    local doc_verb="${2:-}"
    case "$doc_verb" in
      grill|refine|review)
        local doc="$subcmd"
        shift 2
        skill_verb_message "$doc $doc_verb" \
          "Agentic verb — requires an LLM to interview, rewrite, or gate-check ${doc}." \
          "$@"
        ;;
      "")
        # `spectacular <doc>` with no verb — let the skill infer (grill if empty, review if filled)
        local doc="$subcmd"
        shift
        skill_verb_message "$doc" \
          "Agentic dispatch — the skill resolves the right verb from ${doc}'s current state." \
          "$@"
        ;;
      *)
        die "Unknown verb '$doc_verb' for doc '$subcmd'.
Agentic verbs (skill-only):  grill | refine | review
Run inside Claude Code or Codex:  /spectacular $subcmd <verb>"
        ;;
    esac
  fi

  if [[ "$subcmd" != "init" ]]; then
    die "Unknown command: '${subcmd}'.
CLI verbs:   init | doctor | pack | migrate | new | advance | undo | next | snapshot | archive | touch | decide | remember | session | feedback | idea | question | research | spike | spec | wayfind | afk | workspace | id | audit | fix
Read verbs:  summary | requests | request | decisions | decision | memories | memory | sessions | show | progress | paths (v1.8.0+)
Skill verbs (run via /spectacular in your AI agent): status | remember this | verify <slug> | <doc> grill | <doc> refine | <doc> review"
  fi

  shift
  parse_args "$@"

  echo "Spectacular init"
  echo ""

  # ── Detect existing installs + resolve skill scope ──────────────────────────
  # Warn if spectacular is already available (upstream / global / plugin), then
  # decide whether to install. If the user did not pin a scope explicitly, an
  # existing install means we default to 'none' (scaffold only, no redundant copy).
  local existing_installs
  existing_installs="$(detect_existing_installs)"

  if [[ -n "$existing_installs" ]]; then
    info "⚠ spectacular already available via:"
    while IFS=$'\t' read -r label path; do
      [[ -z "$label" ]] && continue
      info "    • ${label}: ${path}"
    done <<< "$existing_installs" || true

    if [[ -z "$OPT_SKILL_SCOPE" ]]; then
      OPT_SKILL_SCOPE="none"
      info "  Skipping skill install. Use --skill-scope project (or global) to force a copy."
    fi
    echo ""
  fi

  # No explicit scope and nothing detected → default to a project-local install.
  [[ -z "$OPT_SKILL_SCOPE" ]] && OPT_SKILL_SCOPE="project"

  if $OPT_UPDATE; then
    update_skill
  fi

  if $OPT_INTERACTIVE; then
    run_interactive
  fi

  [[ -z "$OPT_NAME" ]] && OPT_NAME="$(slug_from_dir)"

  local agents_dir claude_dir lock_ref
  agents_dir="$(agents_skill_dir)"
  claude_dir="$(claude_skill_dir)"
  lock_ref="$(read_lock_ref)"

  # Interactive mode: show final summary, ask for confirmation before any writes
  if $OPT_INTERACTIVE; then
    local doc_set_preview
    doc_set_preview="$(resolve_doc_set)"
    echo "Ready to scaffold:"
    echo "  project:     $OPT_NAME"
    echo "  summary:     ${OPT_SUMMARY:-(none)}"
    echo "  agents-file: $OPT_AGENTS_FILE"
    echo "  kit:         $OPT_KIT"
    echo "  skill-scope: $OPT_SKILL_SCOPE"
    echo "  docs:        $doc_set_preview"
    echo ""
    printf "Proceed? [Y/n]: "
    local confirm
    read -r confirm
    case "${confirm:-y}" in
      y|Y|yes|YES) ;;
      *) echo "Aborted. No files written."; exit 0 ;;
    esac
    echo ""
  fi

  echo "Scaffold:"

  scaffold "$OPT_NAME" "$OPT_SUMMARY" "$OPT_AGENTS_FILE"

  echo ""
  echo "Skill:"

  INSTALLED_REF=""
  AGENTS_SKILL_INSTALLED=""
  CLAUDE_SKILL_INSTALLED=""

  if [[ "$OPT_SKILL_SCOPE" == "none" ]]; then
    skip "skill install skipped (--skill-scope none)"
  elif [[ -n "$lock_ref" && -d "$agents_dir" ]]; then
    skip "${agents_dir}  (${lock_ref}, already installed)"
    skip "${claude_dir}  → symlink"
  else
    install_skill
    info "  installed  ${AGENTS_SKILL_INSTALLED}  (${INSTALLED_REF})"
    info "  symlinked  ${CLAUDE_SKILL_INSTALLED}  → ${AGENTS_SKILL_INSTALLED}"
  fi

  print_summary
}

INSTALLED_REF=""
AGENTS_SKILL_INSTALLED=""
CLAUDE_SKILL_INSTALLED=""

main "$@"
